  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Core Concept**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the core concept: a dual-target strategy for UPSC CAPF AC and SSC CPO. I\'ve broken down the shared elements, which include polity, history, geography, science, and English. The CPO track requires high-speed quant, which I am exploring.\n\n\n**Refining Exam Simulation**\n\nI\'m now integrating exam simulation features. For CPO, I\'m incorporating a timed \"Sprint\" mode with speed tracking. It will have formula breakdowns and shortcut displays. For CAPF, a \"Deep-Dive\" mode is emerging, focusing on multi-statement MCQs and a scratchpad feature for statement elimination. The goal is to accurately mirror both exams.\n\n\n**Developing CAPF Paper 2**\n\nI\'m now focusing on CAPF Paper 2. I\'m building a \"Argument & Structure Lab\" with a timed Markdown/Rich Editor. It includes structure scaffolding: an argument splitter, a report formatter, and a pr\303\251cis word counter. A Gemini AI evaluation API will score the essays, measuring argument depth, objective tone, and structural adherence to the rubric. It aims to develop a tool to teach exam structure, and constitutional backing.\n\n\n**Constructing an AI Tutor**\n\nI\'m now building an AI tutor. This tutor will break down UPSC CAPF and SSC CPO syllabus topics using an interactive bento tree. It will have an \"Easy Mode\" for any sub-topic, with core concepts, analytical angles, and SSC CPO speed. It\'s designed to give actionable suggestions with model answers. I\'m also ensuring integration for personalized practice questions based on learning gaps.\n\n\n**Implementing Practice & Analysis**\n\nI\'m now incorporating practice and analysis tools. I\'m focusing on \"D. Micro-Categorized PYQ Bank & Mistake Vault,\" allowing filtering by subject and micro-topic for past questions and storing incorrect answers in a \"Mistake Vault\" for revision. There will be memory hooks, mnemonics, and formula/trap alerts. I\'m also planning \"E. Unified Syllabus & Daily Routine Tracker,\" with a bento-style dashboard and spaced repetition. The goal is to provide custom drills and track progress on overlapping subjects.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_466335224941635805"
