    thinking: "**Defining Core Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on outlining the fundamental components needed for the DutyDeck architecture. Specifically, I\'m defining core data structures within `src/types/index.ts`. For instance, I\'m thinking about the `ExamTrack` and `Subject` types to categorize the core data. I\'m considering types like `UPSC_CAPF`, `SSC_CPO`, `SHARED_CORE`, and subject options such as `Polity`.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been fleshing out more detailed data structures. I\'m introducing types like `Question`, `Paper2Submission`, `MistakeRecord`, and `SyllabusTopic` to represent the core data units. The `Question` type includes fields for ID, exam targets, subject, difficulty, question text, options, answer, and explanation details. I\'m also including fields for paper 2 submissions, mistake records, and syllabus topics to represent user data and other key concepts.\n\n\n**Developing Core Utilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on core utility functions. I\'ve been working on `cbtEngine.ts` to calculate CBT scores based on exam-specific marking schemes, including speed alerts. Also, I\'m developing statement and option elimination heuristics in `elimination.ts`, including the automatic suggestions. I\'m also planning SRS scheduling and error tagging in `srsVault.ts`, aiming for a flexible system. Finally, I\'m scaffolding paper 2 responses with `paper2Scaffold.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing Test-Driven Logic**\n\nI\'m now writing unit tests in `src/utils/rules.test.ts` using `node:test` to ensure the logic functions are sound. Simultaneously, I\'m working on building a high-quality seed question bank within `src/data/questionBank.ts`, featuring authentic UPSC CAPF AC and SSC CPO questions. I\'m also creating comprehensive syllabus data in `src/data/syllabusData.ts`, incorporating dual exam breakdowns and references. Finally, I\'m defining an Express server in `server.ts` with AI endpoints for syllabus explanations and generation.\n\n\n**Designing AI Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating AI for dynamic question generation and paper 2 evaluation. I\'m working on API endpoints. I am adding AI rubric evaluation for Paper 2 responses and instant explanations of missed questions, based on user-identified mistakes, with focused feedback. I\'m also planning to utilize Vite for development and static serving for production.\n\n\n**Developing New Feature Modes**\n\nI\'m now diving into feature mode implementation. I\'m focusing on defining several core modules. I\'m currently conceptualizing the \"CAPF Elimination Engine,\" which will allow for multi-statement scratchpad functionality, auto-elimination for options, and deep analytical review, supported by citations. In addition, I\'m designing the \"Paper 2 Argument & Structure Lab,\" which is a mode for essay writing. I\'m also planning the \"AI Topic Breakdown & Gap Tutor\", \"Mistake Vault & Spaced Repetition (SRS)\", and \"Bento Overview Dashboard\" modules to manage user data, AI interaction and overall progress.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_7583989024369427824"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"export type ExamTrack = \'UPSC_CAPF\' | \'SSC_CPO\' | \'SHARED_CORE\';\\n\\nexport type Subject = \\n  | \'Polity & Constitution\' \\n  | \'Modern History\' \\n  | \'Geography & Environment\' \\n  | \'General Science\' \\n  | \'Quantitative Aptitude\' \\n  | \'Reasoning & Intelligence\' \\n  | \'English Comprehension\' \\n  | \'Paper 2 (Subjective)\';\\n\\nexport interface QuestionOption {\\n  key: \'A\' | \'B\' | \'C\' | \'D\';\\n  text: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface QuestionExplanation {\\n  coreConcept: string;\\n  shortcutOrTrick?: string;\\n  standardBookRef?: string;\\n  trapAlert?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Question {\\n  id: string;\\n  targetExam: (\'SSC_CPO\' | \'UPSC_CAPF\')[];\\n  subject: Subject;\\n  microTopic: string;\\n  difficulty: \'Speed\' | \'Analytical\';\\n  type: \'SINGLE_CHOICE\' | \'STATEMENT_BASED\';\\n  questionText: string;\\n  statements?: string[]; // 1, 2, 3 statements for UPSC standard format\\n  options: QuestionOption[];\\n  correctAnswer: \'A\' | \'B\' | \'C\' | \'D\';\\n  explanation: QuestionExplanation;\\n  yearRef?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport type MistakeReason = \'Conceptual Gap\' | \'Misread Question\' | \'Calculation/Time Panic\';\\n\\nexport interface MistakeRecord {\\n  id: string;\\n  questionId: string;\\n  selectedAnswer: \'A\' | \'B\' | \'C\' | \'D\';\\n  correctAnswer: \'A\' | \'B\' | \'C\' | \'D\';\\n  timeSpentSeconds: number;\\n  reason?: MistakeReason;\\n  timestamp: number;\\n  reviewCount: number;\\n  nextReviewDate: number; // SRS timestamp\\n  notes?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport type Paper2Type = \'ESSAY\' | \'ARGUMENT\' | \'REPORT\' | \'PRECIS\';\\n\\nexport interface Paper2Prompt {\\n  id: string;\\n  type: Paper2Type;\\n  title: string;\\n  prompt: string;\\n  wordLimit: number;\\n  suggestedMinutes: number;\\n  originalPassage?: string; // For Pr\303\251cis writing\\n  contextTags: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Paper2Feedback {\\n  totalScore: number; // out of 20 marks\\n  structuralScore: number;\\n  factualAndDepthScore: number;\\n  toneAndGrammarScore: number;\\n  objectiveToneAudit: string;\\n  pointsForFeedback: string[];\\n  pointsAgainstFeedback: string[];\\n  pr\303\251cisRuleCompliance?: string;\\n  strengths: string[];\\n  suggestedImprovements: string[];\\n  modelAnswerSnippet?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Paper2Submission {\\n  id: string;\\n  topicType: Paper2Type;\\n  promptId: string;\\n  promptTitle: string;\\n  content: string;\\n  wordCount: number;\\n  timeSpentSeconds: number;\\n  submittedAt: number;\\n  aiFeedback?: Paper2Feedback;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SyllabusSubtopic {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  isShared: boolean;\\n  examFocus: (\'CAPF\' | \'CPO\')[];\\n  weightage: \'High\' | \'Medium\' | \'Low\';\\n  standardRef: string;\\n  keyConcepts: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SyllabusModule {\\n  id: string;\\n  subject: Subject;\\n  iconName: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  isSharedCore: boolean;\\n  subtopics: SyllabusSubtopic[];\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Define shared types for questions, CBT speed engine, Paper 2 submissions, Mistake Vault, and Syllabus modules\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/index.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing type definitions\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create src/types/index.ts\"}"
