  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Utility Modules**\n\nOkay, I\'m now delving into the construction of core utility modules. Specifically, I\'m focusing on `src/utils/cbtEngine.ts`. The initial piece I\'m working on is `calculateCbtScore`, which will tally CBT scores for exams like SSC CPO and UPSC CAPF. Right now, I\'m considering SSC CPO.\n\n\n**Refining Scoring Systems**\n\nI\'m now refining the scoring systems. I\'m building out scoring functions. For SSC CPO, I\'ve got +1 for correct, -0.25 for incorrect, 0 for unattempted. I\'m moving on to UPSC CAPF; it will be +2 for correct, -0.67 for incorrect, 0 for unattempted.\n\nI\'m also working on speed-related utilities. Specifically, I\'m defining `isSpeedWarning(timeSpentSeconds: number, threshold = 45): boolean`, and `formatTimer(seconds: number): string`.\n\nI\'m starting a new utility, `elimination.ts`, which I will use for UPSC-style questions. This will handle eliminating answer choices based on statements.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_15653043410291519859"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"import { Question } from \'../types\';\\n\\nexport interface ScoreSummary {\\n  attempted: number;\\n  correct: number;\\n  incorrect: number;\\n  unattempted: number;\\n  accuracyPercent: number;\\n  netScore: number;\\n  maxScore: number;\\n  speedAlertCount: number; // Questions exceeding 45s\\n}\\n\\nexport function calculateCbtScore(\\n  questions: Question[],\\n  answers: Record<string, \'A\' | \'B\' | \'C\' | \'D\' | undefined>,\\n  questionTimes: Record<string, number>,\\n  examType: \'SSC_CPO\' | \'UPSC_CAPF\'\\n): ScoreSummary {\\n  const marksPerCorrect = examType === \'UPSC_CAPF\' ? 2 : 1;\\n  const negativeMark = examType === \'UPSC_CAPF\' ? 0.67 : 0.25;\\n\\n  let correct = 0;\\n  let incorrect = 0;\\n  let unattempted = 0;\\n  let speedAlertCount = 0;\\n\\n  questions.forEach((q) => {\\n    const userAns = answers[q.id];\\n    const timeSpent = questionTimes[q.id] || 0;\\n\\n    if (timeSpent > 45) {\\n      speedAlertCount++;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (!userAns) {\\n      unattempted++;\\n    } else if (userAns === q.correctAnswer) {\\n      correct++;\\n    } else {\\n      incorrect++;\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  const attempted = correct + incorrect;\\n  const accuracyPercent = attempted > 0 ? Math.round((correct / attempted) * 100) : 0;\\n  const rawNetScore = correct * marksPerCorrect - incorrect * negativeMark;\\n  const netScore = Math.max(0, Math.round(rawNetScore * 100) / 100);\\n  const maxScore = questions.length * marksPerCorrect;\\n\\n  return {\\n    attempted,\\n    correct,\\n    incorrect,\\n    unattempted,\\n    accuracyPercent,\\n    netScore,\\n    maxScore,\\n    speedAlertCount,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function isSpeedWarning(timeSpentSeconds: number, threshold = 45): boolean {\\n  return timeSpentSeconds > threshold;\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatTimer(seconds: number): string {\\n  const mins = Math.floor(seconds / 60);\\n  const secs = seconds % 60;\\n  return `${mins.toString().padStart(2, \'0\')}:${secs.toString().padStart(2, \'0\')}`;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"CBT score calculations, marking scheme rules, speed flags and timer formatters\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/cbtEngine.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing CBT calculation engine\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create src/utils/cbtEngine.ts\"}"
