T11-44-00-841Z.yml)\n```yaml\n- generic [ref=e3]:\n  - banner [ref=e4]:\n    - generic [ref=e5]:\n      - generic [ref=e6]:\n        - generic [ref=e12] [cursor=pointer]:\n          - generic [ref=e13]:\n            - generic [ref=e14]: DutyDeck\n            - generic [ref=e15]: CAPF AC \303\227 CPO\n          - paragraph [ref=e16]: Dual-Target Objective & Subjective Engine\n        - generic [ref=e17]:\n          - generic [ref=e18]:\n            - generic [ref=e21]: \"4\"\n            - text: Day Routine\n          - generic [ref=e22]:\n            - generic [ref=e24]: \"2\"\n            - text: Solved\n          - generic [ref=e25] [cursor=pointer]:\n            - generic [ref=e26]: \"1\"\n            - text: in Vault\n      - navigation [ref=e27]:\n        - button \"Dual Overview\" [ref=e28]\n        - button \"CPO Speed (15m) CBT\" [ref=e33]:\n          - generic [ref=e36]: CPO Speed (15m)\n          - generic [ref=e37]: CBT\n        - button \"CAPF Elimination P1\" [ref=e38]:\n          - generic [ref=e42]: CAPF Elimination\n          - generic [ref=e43]: P1\n        - button \"Paper 2 Lab Descriptive\" [ref=e44]:\n          - generic [ref=e50]: Paper 2 Lab\n          - generic [ref=e51]: Descriptive\n        - button \"AI Syllabus Tutor\" [ref=e52]\n        - button \"Mistake Vault & SRS 1\" [ref=e57]:\n          - generic [ref=e61]: Mistake Vault & SRS\n          - generic [ref=e62]: \"1\"\n  - main [ref=e63]:\n    - generic [ref=e246]:\n      - generic [ref=e253]:\n        - generic [ref=e254]:\n          - heading \"Personal AI Syllabus Tutor\" [level=2] [ref=e255]\n          - generic [ref=e256]: Break Topic Down Easy\n        - paragraph [ref=e257]: Demystifies complex syllabus topics into intuitive mental models, memory hooks, and targeted practice drills.\n      - generic [ref=e258]:\n        - generic [ref=e259]:\n          - generic [ref=e260]:\n            - generic [ref=e261]: \"Subject Category:\"\n            - combobox [ref=e262]:\n              - option \"Polity & Constitution (Shared Core)\" [selected]\n              - option \"Modern History (Shared Core)\"\n              - option \"Quantitative Aptitude\"\n              - option \"Reasoning & Intelligence\"\n              - option \"Geography & Environment (Shared Core)\"\n              - option \"Paper 2 (Subjective)\"\n          - generic [ref=e263]:\n            - generic [ref=e264]: \"Syllabus Sub-Topic:\"\n            - combobox [ref=e265]:\n              - option \"Emergency Provisions (Art 352, 356, 360)\" [selected]\n              - option \"Armed Forces & Fundamental Rights (Art 33, 34, 35)\"\n              - option \"Governor Discretionary Powers & State Executive (Art 163, 174)\"\n              - option \"Preamble, Basic Structure & Amendments (Art 368)\"\n          - generic [ref=e266]:\n            - generic [ref=e267]: \"Dual Target Strategy:\"\n            - generic [ref=e268]:\n              - button \"Dual Mode\" [ref=e269]\n              - button \"CAPF P1/P2\" [ref=e270]\n              - button \"CPO Speed\" [ref=e271]\n        - generic [ref=e272]:\n          - generic [ref=e273]: \"Personal Learning Gap / Specific Doubts (Optional):\"\n          - textbox \"e.g., I keep confusing 1-month parliamentary approval in Art 352 with 2-months in Art 356...\" [ref=e274]\n        - generic [ref=e275]:\n          - generic [ref=e276]:\n            - text: \"Reference:\"\n            - strong [ref=e279]: M. Laxmikanth Ch. 16\n          - button \"Teach Me This Topic (Easy Mode)\" [ref=e281]\n      - generic [ref=e286]:\n        - generic [ref=e287]:\n          - generic [ref=e288]:\n            - text: Conceptual Master Breakdown\n            - heading \"Emergency Provisions (Art 352, 356, 360)\" [level=3] [ref=e289]\n          - generic [ref=e290]: \"M. Laxmikanth (7th Ed.) \342\200\224 Chapter 16: Emergency Provisions\"\n        - generic [ref=e291]:\n          - heading \"1. Core Intuition in 3 Clear Bullets:\" [level=4] [ref=e292]\n          - generic [ref=e295]:\n            - generic [ref=e296]:\n              - generic [ref=e297]: \"#1\"\n              - text: National Emergency (Art 352) transforms India from a federal system into a unitary system without any formal constitutional amendment.\n            - generic [ref=e298]:\n              - generic [ref=e299]: \"#2\"\n              - text: \"Can only be proclaimed on 3 grounds: War, External Aggression, or Armed Rebellion (44th Amendment Act 1978 deleted \\\"Internal Disturbance\\\").\"\n            - generic [ref=e300]:\n              - generic [ref=e301]: \"#3\"\n              - text: Requires approval by both Houses within 1 month (Art 352) by special majority, whereas State Emergency (Art 356) and Financial Emergency (Art 360) give 2 months by simple majority.\n        - generic [ref=e302]:\n          - generic [ref=e303]:\n            - generic [ref=e304]: \"UPSC CAPF Analytical Angle (Paper 1 & 2):\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e310]: Article 352 requires written recommendation of the Union Cabinet (ministers of cabinet rank), not merely the Prime Minister alone. Under Article 358, fundamental rights under Article 19 are automatically suspended only when emergency is declared on grounds of war/external aggression (not armed rebellion). Under Article 359, the President may suspend the right to enforce fundamental rights via court, BUT Articles 20 (protection against conviction) and 21 (right to life and personal liberty) can NEVER be suspended (44th Amendment Act 1978; Minerva Mills case 1980).\n          - generic [ref=e311]:\n            - generic [ref=e312]: \"SSC CPO Speed Formula / Mental Shortcut:\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e316]: \"30-Second CBT Rule: \\\"1-Month vs 2-Months\\\". Article 352 is the deadliest, so Parliament gets only 1 month to approve. Articles 356 and 360 are less urgent, so Parliament gets 2 months. Special majority is needed only for Art 352; simple majority suffices for Art 356 & 360.\"\n        - generic [ref=e317]:\n          - generic [ref=e318]:\n            - generic [ref=e319]: \"High-Yield Memory Hook / Mnemonic:\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e329]: \"Mnemonic: \\\"WAR-20-21-UNTOUCHABLE\\\" (Grounds: War, External Aggression, Armed Rebellion; Arts 20 & 21 can never be touched even during emergency).\"\n          - generic [ref=e330]:\n            - generic [ref=e331]: \"Classic Examiner Negative-Marking Trap:\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e335]: Examiners frequently swap \"written advice of Prime Minister\" for \"written advice of Cabinet\" (it MUST be Cabinet) and claim Art 19 is suspended during Armed Rebellion (it is NOT suspended during armed rebellion).\n        - generic [ref=e336]:\n          - generic [ref=e337]:\n            - heading \"Ready to cement your mastery?\" [level=4] [ref=e338]\n            - paragraph [ref=e339]: Generate 3 targeted practice questions addressing your specific learning gap in this topic.\n          - button \"Generate 3 Practice Questions\" [ref=e340]\n      - generic [ref=e344]:\n        - generic [ref=e345]:\n          - heading \"Targeted AI Practice Drill on \\\"Emergency Provisions (Art 352, 356, 360)\\\"\" [level=3] [ref=e346]\n          - generic [ref=e350]: 3 Questions Generated\n        - generic [ref=e351]:\n          - generic [ref=e352]:\n            - generic [ref=e353]:\n              - generic [ref=e354]: Drill Q1\n              - generic [ref=e355]: Polity & Constitution\n              - generic [ref=e356]: \342\200\242 Analytical\n            - generic [ref=e357]: UPSC_CAPF\n          - paragraph [ref=e358]: \"With reference to the consequences of a National Emergency declared under Article 352, consider the following statements:\"\n          - generic [ref=e359]:\n            - generic [ref=e360]:\n              - strong [ref=e361]: \"1.\"\n              - text: The executive power of the Union extends to directing any State regarding the manner in which its executive power is to be exercised.\n            - generic [ref=e362]:\n              - strong [ref=e363]: \"2.\"\n              - text: The legislative power of the State Legislature is suspended, and Parliament alone can enact laws for the State.\n            - generic [ref=e364]:\n              - strong [ref=e365]: \"3.\"\n              - text: The President can modify the constitutional distribution of revenues between the Union and the States.\n          - generic [ref=e366]:\n            - generic [ref=e368] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e369]: A\n              - generic [ref=e370]: 1 and 2 only\n            - generic [ref=e372] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e373]: B\n              - generic [ref=e374]: 1 and 3 only\n            - generic [ref=e376] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e377]: C\n              - generic [ref=e378]: 2 and 3 only\n            - generic [ref=e380] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e381]: D\n              - generic [ref=e382]: 1, 2 and 3\n          - button \"Check Answer\" [disabled] [ref=e384]\n        - generic [ref=e385]:\n          - generic [ref=e386]:\n            - generic [ref=e387]:\n              - generic [ref=e388]: Drill Q2\n              - generic [ref=e389]: Polity & Constitution\n              - generic [ref=e390]: \342\200\242 Speed\n            - generic [ref=e391]: SSC_CPO / UPSC_CAPF\n          - paragraph [ref=e392]: Under which Constitutional Amendment Act was the approval period for a Proclamation of National Emergency reduced from two months to one month?\n          - generic [ref=e393]:\n            - generic [ref=e395] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e396]: A\n              - generic [ref=e397]: 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976\n            - generic [ref=e399] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e400]: B\n              - generic [ref=e401]: 44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978\n            - generic [ref=e403] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e404]: C\n              - generic [ref=e405]: 52nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1985\n            - generic [ref=e407] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e408]: D\n              - generic [ref=e409]: 86th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2002\n          - button \"Check Answer\" [disabled] [ref=e411]\n        - generic [ref=e412]:\n          - generic [ref=e413]:\n            - generic [ref=e414]:\n              - generic [ref=e415]: Drill Q3\n              - generic [ref=e416]: Polity & Constitution\n              - generic [ref=e417]: \342\200\242 Analytical\n            - generic [ref=e418]: UPSC_CAPF\n          - paragraph [ref=e419]: \"Consider the following statements regarding suspension of Fundamental Rights during emergency:\"\n          - generic [ref=e420]:\n            - generic [ref=e421]:\n              - strong [ref=e422]: \"1.\"\n              - text: Article 358 operates automatically as soon as National Emergency is declared on any ground.\n            - generic [ref=e423]:\n              - strong [ref=e424]: \"2.\"\n              - text: Article 359 requires a specific Presidential Order to suspend the enforcement of designated fundamental rights.\n            - generic [ref=e425]:\n              - strong [ref=e426]: \"3.\"\n              - text: The right to move court for enforcement of Articles 20 and 21 can never be suspended under Article 359.\n          - generic [ref=e427]:\n            - generic [ref=e429] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e430]: A\n              - generic [ref=e431]: 1 and 2 only\n            - generic [ref=e433] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e434]: B\n              - generic [ref=e435]: 2 and 3 only\n            - generic [ref=e437] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e438]: C\n              - generic [ref=e439]: 1 and 3 only\n            - generic [ref=e441] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e442]: D\n              - generic [ref=e443]: 1, 2 