\n              - option \"[ESSAY] Artificial Intelligence in Border Surveillance & Counter-Terrorism\"\n              - option \"[REPORT] Drone Infiltration Along Western Frontier & Counter-UAS Deployments\"\n              - option \"[REPORT] Glacial Outburst Rescue & Disaster Response in Sikkim Himalayas\"\n              - option \"[PRECIS] Civil-Military Relations and Constitutional Supremacy in Democratic Polities\"\n            - generic [ref=e272]:\n              - generic [ref=e273]:\n                - generic [ref=e274]: ARGUMENT\n                - generic [ref=e275]: \"Target: 300 words \342\200\242 20m\"\n              - paragraph [ref=e276]: \"\\\"Write arguments for and against the statement: \\\"Excessive deployment of Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) for state internal security and election duties undermines their primary mandate of external border defense and border guarding.\\\"\\\"\"\n              - generic [ref=e277]:\n                - generic [ref=e278]: MHA Mandate\n                - generic [ref=e279]: Border Security\n                - generic [ref=e280]: Internal Policing\n                - generic [ref=e281]: Federalism\n            - button \"Reset to UPSC ARGUMENT Scaffold\" [ref=e283]\n          - generic [ref=e290]:\n            - generic [ref=e291]:\n              - generic [ref=e292]: Argument Structure Splitter\n              - generic [ref=e293]: 100%\n            - generic [ref=e294]:\n              - generic [ref=e295]: 1. Introduction / Context Defined\n              - generic [ref=e300]: 2. Arguments FOR the Statement\n              - generic [ref=e305]: 3. Arguments AGAINST the Statement\n              - generic [ref=e310]: 4. Balanced Conclusion / Way Forward\n        - generic [ref=e315]:\n          - generic [ref=e316]:\n            - generic [ref=e317]:\n              - generic [ref=e318]: Examination Writing Desk\n              - generic [ref=e323]:\n                - generic [ref=e324]: 108 words\n                - generic [ref=e325]: / 300 max\n            - textbox \"Draft your answer here according to UPSC CAPF Paper 2 structure...\" [ref=e326]: \"### TOPIC: Deploying CAPFs for State Law & Order Undermines Border Security #### 1. Introduction / Context [Briefly define the context, constitutional provisions, or national security/economic background in 2-3 sentences.] #### 2. Arguments FOR the Statement - **Point 1:** [Primary pillar, institutional or operational benefit, empirical data] - **Point 2:** [Constitutional validity or strategic advantage] - **Point 3:** [Long-term societal/administrative impact] #### 3. Arguments AGAINST the Statement - **Point 1:** [Operational vulnerabilities, federalism or human rights concerns] - **Point 2:** [Fiscal burdens or enforcement bottlenecks] - **Point 3:** [Alternative mechanisms or unintended consequences] #### 4. Balanced Conclusion (Way Forward) [Constructive middle ground maintaining institutional equilibrium and constitutional principles.]\"\n            - generic [ref=e327]:\n              - generic [ref=e328]: \"Exam tip: Maintain objective, constitutional diction without partisan or hyperbolic rhetoric.\"\n              - button \"Submit for AI Rubric Evaluation\" [ref=e329]\n          - generic [ref=e334]:\n            - generic [ref=e335]:\n              - generic [ref=e341]:\n                - heading \"UPSC CAPF Paper 2 Evaluation Report\" [level=3] [ref=e342]\n                - paragraph [ref=e343]: Standard official marking out of 20 marks\n              - generic [ref=e344]:\n                - generic [ref=e345]: \"16.5\"\n                - generic [ref=e346]: / 20\n            - generic [ref=e347]:\n              - generic [ref=e348]:\n                - generic [ref=e349]: Structure & Split\n                - generic [ref=e350]: 5.5 / 6\n              - generic [ref=e351]:\n                - generic [ref=e352]: Constitutional & Fact Depth\n                - generic [ref=e353]: 6.5 / 8\n              - generic [ref=e354]