  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Adaptive Algorithm**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the core adaptive algorithm within the question engine. I\'m prioritizing the dynamic adjustment of both complexity and statement depth based on user performance. I\'m considering using a probabilistic model to evaluate and refine these parameters, aiming for a truly personalized and challenging learning experience.\n\n\n**Analyzing Skill Check Implementation**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the implementation of a comprehensive skill check. I\'m focusing on \"ultra-mode\" verification rounds with acceptance checks, decoupled logic/unit testing using `node:test`, and real-browser verification via `computer-use`. I\'m evaluating the necessary architecture of an `AdaptiveEngine` to track user performance and adapt the difficulty of questions and statement depth. I\'m considering metrics such as accuracy rates, average response time versus speed thresholds, and error taxonomy distribution to gauge user proficiency.\n\n\n**Mapping Complexity to Levels**\n\nI\'m now concretely defining the mapping between question complexity, statement depth, and user skill levels. I\'m focusing on Level 1, which will test foundational definitions, and Level 2, aiming for standard UPSC CAPF AC. For Level 1, I\'m defining a structure with 2 statements, a clear binary distinction, and direct citations, while Level 2 will use 3 statements. I\'m also considering metrics like Misread Question Ratio and Time/Calculation Panic Ratio to inform question generation. I\'m starting with a concrete consecutive streak system for adaptations based on performance.\n\n\n**Defining Level 3 Complexity**\n\nI\'m now concretely defining Level 3 questions, the advanced tier. I\'m focusing on high-order conceptual questions with 3-4 multi-layered statements, emulating the UPSC\'s new pattern. These questions involve nuanced legal doctrines, exceptions, and statement combinations to create genuine tests of knowledge. Also, I\'m considering targeted trap injection for specific error types, such as misreading questions or conceptual gaps.\n\n\n**Implementing Adaptive Traps**\n\nI\'m now integrating error-specific question adaptations. I am focusing on questions addressing the 44th Amendment and Article 352 versus Article 356\'s timing discrepancies. I\'m focusing on \"Calculation/Time Panic\" to inject questions with intuitive shortcuts. I\'m also preparing `UserPerformanceProfile` and `AdaptiveAssessment` types in `src/types/index.ts`. I will define these structures to feed into the adaptive engine\'s logic.\n\n\n**Integrating Adaptive Engine**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the adaptive engine\'s logic. I\'m building pure functions within `engine.ts` to compute topic proficiency using mistake records and solved question IDs, feeding this into `determineAdaptiveParameters` which will generate an adaptive assessment. Unit tests are being added to `adaptiveEngine.test.ts` to validate progression, regression, statement count adjustments, and learning gap detection. Also, I\'m working to update the `/api/ai/generate-questions` endpoint in `server.ts` to accept the assessment and performance profiles.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_16724712317786392978"
