  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Adaptive Engine Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design of `src/utils/adaptiveEngine.ts`. The focus is on defining the core algorithmic logic, starting with `calculateTopicProficiency`. My approach involves finding relevant questions based on the topic, incorporating mistake records, solved question IDs, and the question bank itself. I am now considering how micro-topics fit into this assessment.\n\n\n**Analyzing Proficiency & Decisions**\n\nI\'m now refining the `calculateTopicProficiency` function. I\'ve worked out how to track mistakes, attempts, and correct answers, along with error breakdowns. I\'m focusing on calculating the average time spent and consecutive correct/incorrect answers. I am using those metrics to identify the dominant gap. My plan is to base the `determineAdaptiveAssessment` decision rules on a student\'s proficiency, with thresholds like 75% accuracy and consecutive correct answers.\n\n\n**Refining Complexity & Depth**\n\nI\'m now implementing the adaptive logic based on accuracy, attempts, and conceptual gaps. I\'m focusing on the conditions for complexity adjustments. For mastery, high accuracy and streaks will trigger advanced questions with four statements. On the other hand, low accuracy and conceptual gaps necessitate foundational questions with two statements. These refinements are designed to optimize the learning experience.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_3370706196604865569"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"import { Question, MistakeRecord, MistakeReason, TopicProficiency, AdaptiveAssessment, AdaptiveComplexityLevel } from \'../types\';\\n\\n/**\\n * Computes an aspirant\'s performance metrics and learning gaps for a given topic.\\n */\\nexport function calculateTopicProficiency(\\n  topicTitle: string,\\n  mistakes: MistakeRecord[],\\n  solvedIds: string[],\\n  allQuestions: Question[]\\n): TopicProficiency {\\n  // Normalize topic strings for fuzzy matching\\n  const normTopic = topicTitle.toLowerCase();\\n  \\n  // Find questions relevant to this topic\\n  const topicQuestions = allQuestions.filter((q) => {\\n    const qTopic = (q.microTopic || \'\').toLowerCase();\\n    const qSub = (q.subject || \'\').toLowerCase();\\n    const qText = (q.questionText || \'\').toLowerCase();\\n    return (\\n      normTopic.includes(qTopic) ||\\n      qTopic.includes(normTopic) ||\\n      normTopic.split(\' \')[0].toLowerCase().includes(qTopic.split(\' \')[0]) ||\\n      qText.includes(normTopic.slice(0, 10))\\n    );\\n  });\\n\\n  const topicQuestionIds = new Set(topicQuestions.map((q) => q.id));\\n\\n  // Find solved questions in this topic\\n  const attemptedTopicQuestionIds = solvedIds.filter((id) => topicQuestionIds.has(id));\\n  const topicMistakes = mistakes.filter((m) => topicQuestionIds.has(m.questionId));\\n\\n  const totalAttempts = Math.max(attemptedTopicQuestionIds.length, topicMistakes.length);\\n  const incorrectCount = topicMistakes.length;\\n  const correctCount = Math.max(0, totalAttempts - incorrectCount);\\n  const accuracyRate = totalAttempts > 0 ? Math.round((correctCount / totalAttempts) * 100) : 60; // 60% neutral baseline\\n\\n  // Error taxonomy counts\\n  let conceptualGaps = 0;\\n  let misreadCount = 0;\\n  let timePanicCount = 0;\\n  let totalTime = 0;\\n\\n  topicMistakes.forEach((m) => {\\n    totalTime += m.timeSpentSeconds || 45;\\n    if (m.reason === \'Conceptual Gap\') conceptualGaps++;\\n    else if (m.reason === \'Misread Question\') misreadCount++;\\n    else if (m.reason === \'Calculation/Time Panic\') timePanicCount++;\\n    else conceptualGaps++;\\n  });\\n\\n  const averageTimeSeconds = topicMistakes.length > 0 ? Math.round(totalTime / topicMistakes.length) : 42;\\n\\n  // Determine consecutive streak from most recent mistake or solved events\\n  // If recent mistakes exist, consecutive incorrect is at least 1\\n  let consecutiveIncorrect = 0;\\n  let consecutiveCorrect = 0;\\n\\n  if (topicMistakes.length > 0) {\\n    const lastMistakeTime = Math.max(...topicMistakes.map((m) => m.timestamp));\\n    const now = Date.now();\\n    // If mistake happened in last 1 hour, count consecutive incorrect\\n    if (now - lastMistakeTime < 3600000) {\\n      consecutiveIncorrect = Math.min(topicMistakes.length, 3);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  if (totalAttempts >= 2 && incorrectCount === 0) {\\n    consecutiveCorrect = totalAttempts;\\n  } else if (accuracyRate >= 80) {\\n    consecutiveCorrect = Math.max(1, correctCount - incorrectCount);\\n  }\\n\\n  // Dominant learning gap identification\\n  let dominantGap: MistakeReason | \'Pacing\' | \'None\' = \'None\';\\n  if (conceptualGaps > 0 && conceptualGaps >= misreadCount && conceptualGaps >= timePanicCount) {\\n    dominantGap = \'Conceptual Gap\';\\n  } else if (misreadCount > 0 && misreadCount >= conceptualGaps && misreadCount >= timePanicCount) {\\n    dominantGap = \'Misread Question\';\\n  } else if (timePanicCount > 0 && timePanicCount >= conceptualGaps && timePanicCount >= misreadCount) {\\n    dominantGap = \'Calculation/Time Panic\';\\n  } else if (averageTimeSeconds > 60) {\\n    dominantGap = \'Pacing\';\\n  }\\n\\n  // Determine current baseline complexity level and statement depth\\n  let currentLevel: AdaptiveComplexityLevel = \'Standard\';\\n  let statementDepth: 2 | 3 | 4 = 3;\\n\\n  if (accuracyRate >= 75 && consecutiveCorrect >= 2) {\\n    currentLevel = \'Advanced\';\\n    statementDepth = 4;\\n  } else if (accuracyRate < 50 || consecutiveIncorrect >= 2 || (conceptualGaps >= 2 && accuracyRate < 60)) {\\n    currentLevel = \'Foundational\';\\n    statementDepth = 2;\\n  }\\n\\n  const recentOutcomes: (\'CORRECT\' | \'INCORRECT\')[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < correctCount; i++) recentOutcomes.push(\'CORRECT\');\\n  for (let i = 0; i < incorrectCount; i++) recentOutcomes.push(\'INCORRECT\');\\n\\n  return {\\n    topic: topicTitle,\\n    totalAttempts,\\n    correctCount,\\n    accuracyRate,\\n    averageTimeSeconds,\\n    conceptualGaps,\\n    misreadCount,\\n    timePanicCount,\\n    consecutiveCorrect,\\n    consecutiveIncorrect,\\n    currentLevel,\\n    statementDepth,\\n    dominantGap,\\n    recentOutcomes,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Calculates adaptive question generation parameters based on diagnosed proficiency.\\n */\\nexport function determineAdaptiveAssessment(proficiency: TopicProficiency): AdaptiveAssessment {\\n  const { accuracyRate, consecutiveCorrect, consecutiveIncorrect, conceptualGaps, misreadCount, dominantGap, statementDepth, currentLevel } = proficiency;\\n\\n  // 1. Advanced Tier (4 Statements)\\n  if (currentLevel === \'Advanced\' || (accuracyRate >= 75 && consecutiveCorrect >= 2)) {\\n    return {\\n      level: \'Advanced\',\\n      statementDepth: 4,\\n      identifiedGap: dominantGap === \'Misread Question\' \\n        ? \'High accuracy but vulnerable to fine semantic exceptions in multi-statement sets\'\\n        : \'Syllabus mastery established; ready for multi-statement combinatorial elimination\',\\n      trapTypeToInject: dominantGap === \'Misread Question\' ? \'Subtle Qualifier\' : \'Pacing & Elimination\',\\n      rationale: `Aspirant is demonstrating high proficiency (${accuracyRate}% accuracy, ${consecutiveCorrect} consecutive correct). Scaling statement depth to 4 statements to simulate modern high-order UPSC elimination matrices.`,\\n      learningIntervention: \'Deep analytical synthesis: Testing edge-case statutory provisions and overlapping constitutional articles.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // 2. Foundational Tier (2 Statements)\\n  if (currentLevel === \'Foundational\' || accuracyRate < 50 || consecutiveIncorrect >= 2 || conceptualGaps >= 2) {\\n    return {\\n      level: \'Foundational\',\\n      statementDepth: 2,\\n      identifiedGap: dominantGap === \'Conceptual Gap\'\\n        ? \'Fundamental doctrine confusion (e.g. parliamentary approval majorities or amendment years)\'\\n        : dominantGap === \'Misread Question\'\\n        ? \'Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not correct\\\", \\\"only\\\")\'\\n        : \'Inconsistent recall under test pressure\',\\n      trapTypeToInject: dominantGap === \'Misread Question\' ? \'Subtle Qualifier\' : \'Conceptual Contrast\',\\n      rationale: `Diagnostic indicates a learning gap (${conceptualGaps} conceptual gaps logged, ${accuracyRate}% accuracy). Reducing noise to 2 statements with sharp binary contrast to rebuild conceptual certainty.`,\\n      learningIntervention: \'Remedial consolidation: 2-statement binary verification directly anchored in standard textbook citations.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // 3. Standard Tier (3 Statements)\\n  return {\\n    level: \'Standard\',\\n    statementDepth: 3,\\n    identifiedGap: dominantGap !== \'None\' \\n      ? `Periodic slip-ups tagged under \\\"${dominantGap}\\\"`\\n      : \'Calibrated at standard UPSC CAPF AC elimination benchmark\',\\n    trapTypeToInject: dominantGap === \'Misread Question\' \\n      ? \'Subtle Qualifier\' \\n      : dominantGap === \'Conceptual Gap\'\\n      ? \'Conceptual Contrast\'\\n      : \'None\',\\n    rationale: `Balanced baseline performance (${accuracyRate}% accuracy across ${proficiency.totalAttempts} attempts). Serving canonical 3-statement format where 1 elimination eliminates 50% of choices.`,\\n    learningIntervention: \'Standard elimination mastery: Practicing classic 50/50 deduction heuristics.\',\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Formats a rich adaptive instruction for the Gemini prompt or question setter.\\n */\\nexport function buildAdaptivePromptInstruction(assessment: AdaptiveAssessment, topic: string): string {\\n  return `[ADAPTIVE QUESTION ENGINE DIRECTIVE]\\nTarget Complexity: ${assessment.level.toUpperCase()}\\nStatement Count: EXACTLY ${assessment.statementDepth} statements per question.\\nDiagnosed Learning Gap: \\\"${assessment.identifiedGap}\\\"\\nTargeted Trap Directive: Inject \\\"${assessment.trapTypeToInject}\\\" traps.\\nInstructional Objective: ${assessment.learningIntervention}\\n\\nRules for this level:\\n${\\n  assessment.statementDepth === 2\\n    ? `- Generate exactly 2 distinct, high-contrast statements (1 and 2).\\n- Keep statements direct and anchored to fundamental principles from standard books.\\n- The options should be: \\\"A: 1 only\\\", \\\"B: 2 only\\\", \\\"C: Both 1 and 2\\\", \\\"D: Neither 1 nor 2\\\".`\\n    : assessment.statementDepth === 4\\n    ? `- Generate exactly 4 multi-layered statements (1, 2, 3, and 4) covering constitutional nuances, commission reports, or border jurisdictions.\\n- Require multi-step elimination (e.g., options like \\\"1 and 3 only\\\", \\\"1, 2 and 4 only\\\", \\\"2, 3 and 4 only\\\", \\\"All four\\\").\\n- Provide an intricate elimination clue in the explanation.`\\n    : `- Generate standard 3 statements (1, 2, and 3).\\n- Options should follow classic UPSC format: \\\"1 and 2 only\\\", \\\"2 and 3 only\\\", \\\"1 and 3 only\\\", \\\"1, 2 and 3\\\".\\n- Ensure 1 statement is definitively falsifiable via a known rule.`\\n}`;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Adaptive question engine algorithm that monitors user proficiency, adjusts complexity level, statement depth (2, 3, or 4 statements), and injects targeted traps\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/adaptiveEngine.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing adaptive engine logic\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create src/utils/adaptiveEngine.ts\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\245\034\n\242\034\001i\024}\023\315\376\230\214?d\310\364&Tt\351\220\362\020d\2559\351a<\207\325l\322\233S7\231\276\241\201\207\367\f\244\277\364n\372\237\212+]B x\'%4oH\302{\004\000\347\326\374D<\322/\304\024\260\345\322\200\224\241\037\342D5\017<\213\017_-\344@O\322\202\221AY\261;\342\341\3173<(T1\330\306,\322\f6\b*;\000do\330\332\331\357o-z\234|H\360\251O\260_\276\000\\\203\002:\026-\273\rr\320@\3329\006\277\020\227\217\216\275E\357\360\3313\202\231\260f\223\356\320\356\375\026\320\371{\366X\020\353\255\002\200\357y;sOWZ\226\3609t\177<\377\307\v\021\300;\323\247[\240>.\362rV\2061^\035Q\372\306\336\254\341H\222\321\016D\202p\323~\211~R\270\032\201\270\356\021\233\034\372\177\347\204\300\350\302\377\177t\324r\371\'\221\221G\253\021\335\375\215\372J\277\213\305\211\'\207\247\"\225V\212>\0359\252+L\v\317\355\226(\203\327\271\3448A\331|\033\227\257\326\227\223\263\037\320\356Mx)\317\300\267\037K>\006M\226\344JZ64\334(4\331+\207\247<\276\363\326\321\317\263\323-\n\324,\375Q\354\201d\200\360\024\01729\327\332\207\235n?\240\307|\224Z#h\257\354l\325\347-|\316\2546\024\210\317\220\003\252q\365cP\235Y\n\v\216\256*\a\273R\211\363\327\362\330\217\342\213\253\016\200\373\201\316\"q\256\321\302\271\262\3533\370I6R\275\212\270z\311@a\357\265\344\333\330\351\n1u\206\r\336Kk\024\345\005\361^\r\016R\221\365\275\247\027@\333j\227m\361\372\303\252\245\2775\262\231\225\343\313\376JZ\333\026\r\356/\271\265h\254F4%_|\253\241y\342\205\226\030\263ZK\022\\@\346\353\270@\323\006\006\332\210\325~|\253^\237)\\y#\237L\025\030,\304AQ9\031\030\336\366\357>;=\\\202\023\\\206A\220<\305\240\343L6O\355\211\316/K^\271\222r\270(\336j\344\005$\235\0252\323\352Y\367\020\350\027\236\006G\032\345\002\230\241+\360\212\345\261\224\236}\024\302\031)}\272mo\206_\3618?\264Iu\0367\321\306\037\005\021\216\237\231z\222\273L\262\201r\232\\E\n\377\v#\363\a\334\303\001ly\343-\332\332\025n\324b\301\251\227\235\315xW\r\210X\217\351%\233\002\335\t F\230\320\232\004\302]\370R\2041\241\365\032\"\367\b\252\005R\321A\366\231|\016\221\v\274\241\354\351b\222c\341&\2250\215TF\3373y\314\332\031ct0e\312\344\262\2105\363~\240\005\347\303\202\235\301T\246\005\"\271\213\221X,\253\260\375V\247\252jLp\242\360c\2152\206\332D\315k\034\371O7$j\355\bo\205\310\304\332\334\232/L\032\203\375.p\337\320\303\233\374\360\220V\332\257\327\225\017H<^\334u\346\232\322r*]Q\"\205O\021\324>\005\023\270\037\375v\031\352\330\"o\255\033\357\210a\210iB\016\311.\260\vH\\*\r\000P\215jP\353X\236\211u\r\"P\247\326\037\023c ;\341\242\230\261\344bj=\365gT\001\036\320.G\345\026\221\335~\353\375,Q\207\327\301\255HQ|\327\324G\375\233k\246\253\001\3769j\201\025\222T\000\004n\276\037\250W\241nb\262\354\317\3706^]\327\362y\214p\203\243\304\340/\027\265\372\303b\221K\2031Dy\254P\271\236\365ss\023\334_\351m\027r\002\200\000\033\351m\243\355\3017)\365\343TA\222\310[V[<N\240?YY\262\352\\\236k\244\001ka\313e\335\337\325\373$\210p2,rKu\\\004\346bo\343n\347\0231\0006t\264\030\355\352\203\350\3507\323a\236\032\020q\232\025\004b\207\002\323\352[\030\235H\256\325\263z$R\235\345\336y;\314\301;b\325\300\310\021\311\333\275\t\364gk\233y\002wNd_\232(\351\212\326\001\357\341\336\252\330(\021v\261\323i\335\362\022Q,U{\035Z\235\337\257\277Kei \357\234\3474\306:x\243\253\226\367\371.\362\354?\034\213\203\004\263\314\363M\212\201\267S\033\244J\025\026>\353\\\313\n\260hE\277.\314P[\304i\231\340\233E\333\020QTZ\213\212`\023\3741\323\005T\221\212%E\345\366\203\265\341\267\266\355\306\244\021\231\342D\261e+\360\333\"\3426\016xg\313\264\2732\006la@\230$}2\360\242\326\024\2142\222\025\v%>\ag\t\201\345\326\255\261\214\000\3023\314\344\303\020\364\026\330A\365N\305\026\264z==\367\353U\354Q\211\320\317m\251\203\326\362\036\366\331\2527\027\241\231\024\034?\312J\347\033\244z\333U\321\322\254\003}\324\232\362\3127\367\025\n\256N\266k\360\232\002dn\203\223\306\225\311\343\247\327\216\303/\237\206]/z\230\317^\247\"=\310\207\225\273I\267T\230w\301\022z\223\006\353\037\032P\341\252*\367\'A\3372\1774\250\366\223\375\367\355#\034