n \"Paper 2 (Subjective)\"\n          - generic [ref=e314]:\n            - generic [ref=e315]: \"Syllabus Sub-Topic:\"\n            - combobox [ref=e316]:\n              - option \"Emergency Provisions (Art 352, 356, 360)\" [selected]\n              - option \"Armed Forces & Fundamental Rights (Art 33, 34, 35)\"\n              - option \"Governor Discretionary Powers & State Executive (Art 163, 174)\"\n              - option \"Preamble, Basic Structure & Amendments (Art 368)\"\n          - generic [ref=e317]:\n            - generic [ref=e318]: \"Dual Target Strategy:\"\n            - generic [ref=e319]:\n              - button \"Dual Mode\" [ref=e320]\n              - button \"CAPF P1/P2\" [ref=e321]\n              - button \"CPO Speed\" [ref=e322]\n        - generic [ref=e323]:\n          - generic [ref=e324]: \"Personal Learning Gap / Specific Doubts (Auto-populated from monitor):\"\n          - \'textbox \"Auto-target: \\\"Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not correct\\\", \\\"only\\\")\\\"\" [ref=e325]\'\n        - generic [ref=e326]:\n          - generic [ref=e327]:\n            - text: \"Reference:\"\n            - strong [ref=e330]: M. Laxmikanth Ch. 16\n          - button \"Teach Me This Topic (Easy Mode)\" [ref=e332]\n      - generic [ref=e337]:\n        - generic [ref=e338]:\n          - generic [ref=e339]:\n            - text: Conceptual Master Breakdown\n            - heading \"Emergency Provisions (Art 352, 356, 360)\" [level=3] [ref=e340]\n          - generic [ref=e341]: \"M. Laxmikanth (7th Ed.) \342\200\224 Chapter 16: Emergency Provisions\"\n        - generic [ref=e342]:\n          - heading \"1. Core Intuition in 3 Clear Bullets:\" [level=4] [ref=e343]\n          - generic [ref=e346]:\n            - generic [ref=e347]:\n              - generic [ref=e348]: \"#1\"\n              - text: National Emergency (Art 352) transforms India from a federal system into a unitary system without any formal constitutional amendment.\n            - generic [ref=e349]:\n              - generic [ref=e350]: \"#2\"\n              - text: \"Can only be proclaimed on 3 grounds: War, External Aggression, or Armed Rebellion (44th Amendment Act 1978 deleted \\\"Internal Disturbance\\\").\"\n            - generic [ref=e351]:\n              - generic [ref=e352]: \"#3\"\n              - text: Requires approval by both Houses within 1 month (Art 352) by special majority, whereas State Emergency (Art 356) and Financial Emergency (Art 360) give 2 months by simple majority.\n        - generic [ref=e353]:\n          - generic [ref=e354]:\n            - generic [ref=e355]: \"UPSC CAPF Analytical Angle (Paper 1 & 2):\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e361]: Article 352 requires written recommendation of the Union Cabinet (ministers of cabinet rank), not merely the Prime Minister alone. Under Article 358, fundamental rights under Article 19 are automatically suspended only when emergency is declared on grounds of war/external aggression (not armed rebellion). Under Article 359, the President may suspend the right to enforce fundamental rights via court, BUT Articles 20 (protection against conviction) and 21 (right to life and personal liberty) can NEVER be suspended (44th Amendment Act 1978; Minerva Mills case 1980).\n          - generic [ref=e362]:\n            - generic [ref=e363]: \"SSC CPO Speed Formula / Mental Shortcut:\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e367]: \"30-Second CBT Rule: \\\"1-Month vs 2-Months\\\". Article 352 is the deadliest, so Parliament gets only 1 month to approve. Articles 356 and 360 are less urgent, so Parliament gets 2 months. Special majority is needed only for Art 352; simple majority suffices for Art 356 & 360.\"\n        - generic [ref=e368]:\n          - generic [ref=e369]:\n            - generic [ref=e370]: \"High-Yield Memory Hook / Mnemonic:\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e380]: \"Mnemonic: \\\"WAR-20-21-UNTOUCHABLE\\\" (Grounds: War, External Aggression, Armed Rebellion; Arts 20 & 21 can never be touched even during emergency).\"\n          - generic [ref=e381]:\n            - generic [ref=e382]: \"Classic Examiner Negative-Marking Trap:\"\n            - paragraph [ref=e386]: Examiners frequently swap \"written advice of Prime Minister\" for \"written advice of Cabinet\" (it MUST be Cabinet) and claim Art 19 is suspended during Armed Rebellion (it is NOT suspended during armed rebellion).\n        - generic [ref=e387]:\n          - generic [ref=e388]:\n            - generic [ref=e389]:\n              - heading \"Generate Practice Questions (Calibrated to Current Gap)\" [level=4] [ref=e390]\n              - generic [ref=e391]: 2 Statements\n            - paragraph [ref=e392]:\n              - text: \"Engine will generate questions specifically addressing:\"\n              - generic [ref=e393]: \"\\\"Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not correct\\\", \\\"only\\\")\\\"\"\n          - button \"Generate 2-Statement Drill\" [ref=e394]\n      - generic [ref=e398]:\n        - generic [ref=e399]:\n          - \'heading \"Adaptively Calibrated Drill (2 Statements \342\200\242 Level: Foundational)\" [level=3] [ref=e403]\'\n          - generic [ref=e404]: \"Tuned to: Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not...\"\n        - generic [ref=e405]:\n          - generic [ref=e406]:\n            - generic [ref=e407]:\n              - generic [ref=e408]: Adaptive Q1\n              - generic [ref=e409]: Polity & Constitution\n              - generic [ref=e410]: \342\200\242 2 Statements\n            - generic [ref=e411]: \"Adaptive Level: Foundational (2 Stmts)\"\n          - paragraph [ref=e412]: \"Consider the following two statements regarding National Emergency under Article 352 (Foundational Diagnostic):\"\n          - generic [ref=e413]:\n            - generic [ref=e414]:\n              - strong [ref=e415]: \"1.\"\n              - text: A proclamation of National Emergency can only be issued upon the written advice of the Union Cabinet (not Prime Minister alone).\n            - generic [ref=e416]:\n              - strong [ref=e417]: \"2.\"\n              - text: The proclamation must be approved by each House of Parliament within two months from its date of issue.\n          - generic [ref=e418]:\n            - generic [ref=e420] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e421]: A\n              - generic [ref=e422]: 1 only\n            - generic [ref=e424] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e425]: B\n              - generic [ref=e426]: 2 only\n            - generic [ref=e428] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e429]: C\n              - generic [ref=e430]: Both 1 and 2\n            - generic [ref=e432] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e433]: D\n              - generic [ref=e434]: Neither 1 nor 2\n          - button \"Check Answer\" [disabled] [ref=e436]\n        - generic [ref=e437]:\n          - generic [ref=e438]:\n            - generic [ref=e439]:\n              - generic [ref=e440]: Adaptive Q2\n              - generic [ref=e441]: Polity & Constitution\n              - generic [ref=e442]: \342\200\242 2 Statements\n            - generic [ref=e443]: \"Adaptive Level: Foundational (2 Stmts)\"\n          - paragraph [ref=e444]: \"Consider the following two statements regarding Article 358 and Article 359:\"\n          - generic [ref=e445]:\n            - generic [ref=e446]:\n              - strong [ref=e447]: \"1.\"\n              - text: Article 358 operates automatically to suspend Article 19 freedoms as soon as emergency is declared on grounds of Armed Rebellion.\n            - generic [ref=e448]:\n              - strong [ref=e449]: \"2.\"\n              - text: Under Article 359, the enforcement of Articles 20 and 21 can never be suspended by Presidential Order.\n          - generic [ref=e450]:\n            - generic [ref=e452] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e453]: A\n              - generic [ref=e454]: 1 only\n            - generic [ref=e456] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e457]: B\n              - generic [ref=e458]: 2 only\n            - generic [ref=e460] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e461]: C\n              - generic [ref=e462]: Both 1 and 2\n            - generic [ref=e464] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - generic [ref=e465]: D\n              - generic [ref=e466]: Neither 1 nor 2\n          - button \"Check Answer\" [disabled] [ref=e468]\n  - contentinfo [ref=e240]:\n    - generic [ref=e241]:\n      - generic [ref=e242]:\n        - generic [ref=e243]: DutyDeck\n        - generic [ref=e244]: \342\200\242 Dual-Target Preparation Engine for UPSC CAPF AC & SSC CPO\n      - generic [ref=e245]: Nordic Botanical Theme \342\200\242 15-Minute Section Gates \342\200\242 Elimination Scratchpad\n```\n\n### Log (.playwright-cli/console-2026-11-12T12-12-00-092Z.log#L1-L1)\n```\n[     764ms] [INFO] %cDownload the React DevTools for a better development experience: https://react.dev/link/react-devtools font-weight:bold @ http://localhost:3000/node_modules/.vite/deps/react-dom_client.js?v=88752353:15801\n```\n\n<attached-media>\nimage/png /.aistudio/artifacts/brain/11de2bb8-3d03-41f4-b9b1-31ec81e6ffef/.tempmediaStorage/r13-adaptive-hud-and-drill.png\n</attached-media>\n"
