  planner_response {
    response: "### Adaptive Difficulty & Statement-Depth Algorithm Implemented\n\nAn adaptive intelligence layer has been integrated into the **DutyDeck** question engine that continuously tracks an aspirant\'s performance history and automatically adjusts the complexity, statement depth, and trap design of generated **UPSC CAPF practice questions**.\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural Components\n\n#### 1. Real-Time Performance & Gap Profiling (`src/utils/adaptiveEngine.ts`)\n- **Telemetry Monitored**:\n  - **Topic Mastery Rate**: Rolling percentage of correct vs. incorrect answers for the selected syllabus sub-topic.\n  - **Consecutive Streak Tracking**: Tracks consecutive correct answers vs. repeat mistakes.\n  - **Error Taxonomy Dominance**: Analyzes the distribution of tagged errors (**Conceptual Gap**, **Misread Question**, or **Calculation/Time Panic**).\n  - **Pacing Metrics**: Average response time per question (flags over-deliberation $>60$s).\n\n#### 2. Three-Tier Complexity & Statement Depth Mapping\nThe engine dynamically maps the diagnosed proficiency into three structural tiers:\n\n| Adaptive Tier | Trigger Conditions | Statement Depth | Elimination & Option Structure | Targeted Intervention |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **Foundational (Remedial)** | Accuracy $<50\\%$, 2+ consecutive errors, or $\\ge 2$ conceptual gaps | **2 Statements** | Clean binary contrast: `1 only`, `2 only`, `Both 1 and 2`, `Neither 1 nor 2`. | Removes cognitive noise; anchors directly to core book definitions (*Laxmikanth / Spectrum*). |\n| **Standard (CAPF AC Benchmark)** | Balanced accuracy ($50\\% - 74\\%$) or initial topic exploration | **3 Statements** | Classic UPSC elimination: 1 false statement eliminates $50\\%$ of options. | Balances speed with deductive elimination practice. |\n| **Advanced (High-Order Mastery)** | Accuracy $\\ge 75\\%$ AND consecutive streak $\\ge 2$ | **4 Statements** | Multi-combinatorial options (`1, 2 and 4 only`, `All four`, etc.). | Tests edge-case statutory provisions, overlapping articles (e.g. Art 358 vs 359), and Supreme Court doctrines (*Minerva Mills*, *Bommai*). |\n\n#### 3. Targeted Trap Injection\n- **Misread Question Gap**: Injects subtle qualifying traps (e.g., *\"President proclaims emergency on advice of Prime Minister alone\"* or *\"State Legislatures may also restrict rights under Art 33\"*).\n- **Conceptual Gap**: Injects high-contrast statement pairs between easily conflated articles or amendment acts (e.g., 42nd vs. 44th Amendment Act, 1-month vs. 2-month parliamentary approval).\n- **Time/Panic Gap**: Injects questions requiring 1-step deductive shortcuts.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Summary\n\n1. **Unit Tests (`src/utils/adaptiveEngine.test.ts`)**:\n   - Verified that detecting $\\ge 2$ conceptual gaps immediately scales statement depth down to **2 statements** with conceptual contrast traps.\n   - Verified that high accuracy ($\\ge 75\\%$) and a positive streak scales statement depth up to **4 statements**.\n   - Verified that misread question records trigger subtle qualifier traps.\n   - All **10 unit tests** passed cleanly in **492ms** (`npx --yes tsx --test`).\n\n2. **Browser Verification (`playwright-cli`)**:\n   - Navigated to **AI Syllabus Tutor**.\n   - Verified the **Adaptive Learning Gap & Statement Depth Monitor** HUD correctly identified the active learning gap (*\"Careless reading of negative qualifiers\"*).\n   - Generated an adaptive drill and verified that each question contained **exactly 2 statements** with foundational binary options (`1 only`, `2 only`, `Both`, `Neither`).\n   - Verified clean TypeScript compilation and dev server execution."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Algorithm Execution**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started examining the algorithm\'s execution on that image you provided. I see a seed mistake logged under \"Misread Question\" for Emergency Provisions. The Adaptive Monitor promptly noted a 0% Topic Mastery Trend and a Statement Depth of 2. I\'m focusing on how these data points influenced subsequent actions.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Adaptive Difficulty & Statement-Depth Algorithm Implemented\n\nAn adaptive intelligence layer has been integrated into the **DutyDeck** question engine that continuously tracks an aspirant\'s performance history and automatically adjusts the complexity, statement depth, and trap design of generated **UPSC CAPF practice questions**.\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural Components\n\n#### 1. Real-Time Performance & Gap Profiling (`src/utils/adaptiveEngine.ts`)\n- **Telemetry Monitored**:\n  - **Topic Mastery Rate**: Rolling percentage of correct vs. incorrect answers for the selected syllabus sub-topic.\n  - **Consecutive Streak Tracking**: Tracks consecutive correct answers vs. repeat mistakes.\n  - **Error Taxonomy Dominance**: Analyzes the distribution of tagged errors (**Conceptual Gap**, **Misread Question**, or **Calculation/Time Panic**).\n  - **Pacing Metrics**: Average response time per question (flags over-deliberation $>60$s).\n\n#### 2. Three-Tier Complexity & Statement Depth Mapping\nThe engine dynamically maps the diagnosed proficiency into three structural tiers:\n\n| Adaptive Tier | Trigger Conditions | Statement Depth | Elimination & Option Structure | Targeted Intervention |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **Foundational (Remedial)** | Accuracy $<50\\%$, 2+ consecutive errors, or $\\ge 2$ conceptual gaps | **2 Statements** | Clean binary contrast: `1 only`, `2 only`, `Both 1 and 2`, `Neither 1 nor 2`. | Removes cognitive noise; anchors directly to core book definitions (*Laxmikanth / Spectrum*). |\n| **Standard (CAPF AC Benchmark)** | Balanced accuracy ($50\\% - 74\\%$) or initial topic exploration | **3 Statements** | Classic UPSC elimination: 1 false statement eliminates $50\\%$ of options. | Balances speed with deductive elimination practice. |\n| **Advanced (High-Order Mastery)** | Accuracy $\\ge 75\\%$ AND consecutive streak $\\ge 2$ | **4 Statements** | Multi-combinatorial options (`1, 2 and 4 only`, `All four`, etc.). | Tests edge-case statutory provisions, overlapping articles (e.g. Art 358 vs 359), and Supreme Court doctrines (*Minerva Mills*, *Bommai*). |\n\n#### 3. Targeted Trap Injection\n- **Misread Question Gap**: Injects subtle qualifying traps (e.g., *\"President proclaims emergency on advice of Prime Minister alone\"* or *\"State Legislatures may also restrict rights under Art 33\"*).\n- **Conceptual Gap**: Injects high-contrast statement pairs between easily conflated articles or amendment acts (e.g., 42nd vs. 44th Amendment Act, 1-month vs. 2-month parliamentary approval).\n- **Time/Panic Gap**: Injects questions requiring 1-step deductive shortcuts.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Summary\n\n1. **Unit Tests (`src/utils/adaptiveEngine.test.ts`)**:\n   - Verified that detecting $\\ge 2$ conceptual gaps immediately scales statement depth down to **2 statements** with conceptual contrast traps.\n   - Verified that high accuracy ($\\ge 75\\%$) and a positive streak scales statement depth up to **4 statements**.\n   - Verified that misread question records trigger subtle qualifier traps.\n   - All **10 unit tests** passed cleanly in **492ms** (`npx --yes tsx --test`).\n\n2. **Browser Verification (`playwright-cli`)**:\n   - Navigated to **AI Syllabus Tutor**.\n   - Verified the **Adaptive Learning Gap & Statement Depth Monitor** HUD correctly identified the active learning gap (*\"Careless reading of negative qualifiers\"*).\n   - Generated an adaptive drill and verified that each question contained **exactly 2 statements** with foundational binary options (`1 only`, `2 only`, `Both`, `Neither`).\n   - Verified clean TypeScript compilation and dev server execution."
