  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Configuration UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating a configuration UI into the AI Tutor component. My primary objective is to enable users to manually adjust the \"Statement Depth\" parameter. This will allow them to control the complexity of the questions generated, from simple factual recall up to multi-statement, four-part questions.\n\n\n**Refining Statement Depth**\n\nI\'ve updated the statement depth range in the Gemini API integration to accommodate 1 to 4 statements, aligning with different question complexity levels. I\'m focusing on these categories: Single-statement factual recall, binary comparison, canonical UPSC CAPF elimination, and complex UPSC-style analysis. I also need to update the AI generation logic to respect the user\'s chosen depth setting.\n\n\n**Expanding Statement Depth Range**\n\nI\'ve expanded the `statementDepth` type to include \"1\", representing direct factual recall questions. I\'m modifying `determineAdaptiveAssessment` and `buildAdaptivePromptInstruction` to handle this. It involves single-statement prompts, eliminating the need for a statements array, with four direct answer options, which will lead to a SINGLE_CHOICE question type. Now I am working on the other depths.\n\n\n**Implementing Factual Recall**\n\nI\'m now fully implementing the factual recall option (`statementDepth === 1`). The system instruction and prompt are updated to generate direct, CBT-style factual questions with four distinct options. I\'ve also implemented a fallback handler for this depth, focusing on high-yield recall questions. Simultaneously, I\'m integrating a Statement Depth Selector UI with four intuitive buttons, to improve the user experience. I\'m focusing on ensuring all the statement depth options are respected.\n\n\n"
