  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Depth Parameters**\n\nI\'m adjusting the depth parameters in `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m modifying the `manualDepth` state in the component. I\'m expanding the allowed depth levels to include 1, rather than starting at a depth of 2. I\'m also examining the `effectiveAssessment` within the same file for potential adaptions.\n\n\n**Expanding Depth Options**\n\nI\'ve been working on the UI to control statement depth, expanding it to include level 1. I\'m focusing on a dedicated controller in the HUD tile. I\'m aiming for clarity in options: \"1 Stmt (Factual Recall)\", \"2 Stmts (Foundational)\", etc. I\'m ensuring the AI respects the new user-defined depth setting. My objective is to achieve a user-friendly and intuitive control system for question complexity.\n\n\n**Defining Depth Categories**\n\nI\'m now categorizing statement depths for clarity. I\'m introducing descriptions for levels 1-4: \"Direct Factual Recall,\" \"Remedial Contrast,\" \"Canonical Elimination,\" and \"Advanced Analysis.\" Clicking a depth button will also enable manual override for direct control or toggling. I\'m updating the question display to accurately reflect the statement count and adapting the server logic for single-statement questions.\n\n\n"
