  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Statement Depth**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to best visualize \"Statement Depth\" within the HUD Tile 2 in `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. My current thought is to render a \"Statement Depth\" header, along with a badge displaying the current depth using the format `{effectiveAssessment.statementDepth} Stmt{effectiveAssessment.statementDepth === 1 ? \'\' : \'s\'}`. This should provide a clear and concise representation of the current depth level.\n\n\n**Implementing Depth Controls**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to offer manual control over statement depth. My plan involves a 4-button grid, either numbered or labeled with descriptive terms like \"Factual\" and \"Complex.\" Clicking a button toggles a manual override and sets the `manualDepth`. I\'ll also add a subtitle providing context for each depth level. Further, I plan to integrate this depth selector directly into the \"Generate Practice Questions\" trigger box, offering the user control even after seeing the breakdown.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
