    combined_output {
      full: "<truncated 21 bytes>\ning Gap / Specific Doubts (Auto-populated from monitor):\"          - \'textbox \"Auto-target: \\\"Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not correct\\\", \\\"only\\\")\\\"\" [ref=e326]\'        - generic [ref=e327]:          - generic [ref=e328]:            - text: \"Reference:\"            - strong [ref=e331]: M. Laxmikanth Ch. 16          - button \"Teach Me This Topic (Easy Mode)\" [ref=e333]      - generic [ref=e338]:        - generic [ref=e339]:          - generic [ref=e340]:            - text: Conceptual Master Breakdown            - heading \"Emergency Provisions (Art 352, 356, 360)\" [level=3] [ref=e341]          - generic [ref=e342]: \"M. Laxmikanth (7th Ed.) \342\200\224 Chapter 16: Emergency Provisions\"        - generic [ref=e343]:          - heading \"1. Core Intuition in 3 Clear Bullets:\" [level=4] [ref=e344]          - generic [ref=e347]:            - generic [ref=e348]:              - generic [ref=e349]: \"#1\"              - text: National Emergency (Art 352) transforms India from a federal system into a unitary system without any formal constitutional amendment.            - generic [ref=e350]:              - generic [ref=e351]: \"#2\"              - text: \"Can only be proclaimed on 3 grounds: War, External Aggression, or Armed Rebellion (44th Amendment Act 1978 deleted \\\"Internal Disturbance\\\").\"            - generic [ref=e352]:              - generic [ref=e353]: \"#3\"              - text: Requires approval by both Houses within 1 month (Art 352) by special majority, whereas State Emergency (Art 356) and Financial Emergency (Art 360) give 2 months by simple majority.        - generic [ref=e354]:          - generic [ref=e355]:            - generic [ref=e356]: \"UPSC CAPF Analytical Angle (Paper 1 & 2):\"            - paragraph [ref=e362]: Article 352 requires written recommendation of the Union Cabinet (ministers of cabinet rank), not merely the Prime Minister alone. Under Article 358, fundamental rights under Article 19 are automatically suspended only when emergency is declared on grounds of war/external aggression (not armed rebellion). Under Article 359, the President may suspend the right to enforce fundamental rights via court, BUT Articles 20 (protection against conviction) and 21 (right to life and personal liberty) can NEVER be suspended (44th Amendment Act 1978; Minerva Mills case 1980).          - generic [ref=e363]:            - generic [ref=e364]: \"SSC CPO Speed Formula / Mental Shortcut:\"            - paragraph [ref=e368]: \"30-Second CBT Rule: \\\"1-Month vs 2-Months\\\". Article 352 is the deadliest, so Parliament gets only 1 month to approve. Articles 356 and 360 are less urgent, so Parliament gets 2 months. Special majority is needed only for Art 352; simple majority suffices for Art 356 & 360.\"        - generic [ref=e369]:          - generic [ref=e370]:            - generic [ref=e371]: \"High-Yield Memory Hook / Mnemonic:\"            - paragraph [ref=e381]: \"Mnemonic: \\\"WAR-20-21-UNTOUCHABLE\\\" (Grounds: War, External Aggression, Armed Rebellion; Arts 20 & 21 can never be touched even during emergency).\"          - generic [ref=e382]:            - generic [ref=e383]: \"Classic Examiner Negative-Marking Trap:\"            - paragraph [ref=e387]: Examiners frequently swap \"written advice of Prime Minister\" for \"written advice of Cabinet\" (it MUST be Cabinet) and claim Art 19 is suspended during Armed Rebellion (it is NOT suspended during armed rebellion).        - generic [ref=e388]:          - generic [ref=e389]:            - generic [ref=e390]:              - generic [ref=e391]:                - heading \"Generate Practice Questions (Calibrated to Current Gap)\" [level=4] [ref=e392]                - generic [ref=e393]: 1 Statement (Factual Recall)              - paragraph [ref=e394]:                - text: \"Engine will generate questions specifically addressing:\"                - generic [ref=e395]: \"\\\"Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not correct\\\", \\\"only\\\")\\\"\"            - button \"Generate 1-Statement Drill\" [ref=e418]          - generic [ref=e400]:            - generic [ref=e401]:              - generic [ref=e402]: \"Select Statement Depth:\"              - generic [ref=e403]: Single-statement direct factual recall (CBT objective format)            - generic [ref=e404]:              - button \"1 Stmt (Factual Recall) Direct CBT Recall\" [ref=e405] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e406]: 1 Stmt (Factual Recall)                - generic [ref=e407]: Direct CBT Recall              - button \"2 Stmts (Foundational) Binary Contrast\" [ref=e408] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e409]: 2 Stmts (Foundational)                - generic [ref=e410]: Binary Contrast              - button \"3 Stmts (Standard UPSC) Standard Elimination\" [ref=e411] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e412]: 3 Stmts (Standard UPSC)                - generic [ref=e413]: Standard Elimination              - button \"4 Stmts (Complex Analysis) Multi-Combinatorial\" [ref=e414] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e415]: 4 Stmts (Complex Analysis)                - generic [ref=e416]: Multi-Combinatorial      - generic [ref=e419]:        - generic [ref=e420]:          - \'heading \"Adaptively Calibrated Drill (1 Statement (Factual Recall) \342\200\242 Level: Factual Recall)\" [level=3] [ref=e424]\'          - generic [ref=e425]: \"Tuned to: Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not...\"        - generic [ref=e426]:          - generic [ref=e427]:            - generic [ref=e428]:              - generic [ref=e429]: Adaptive Q1              - generic [ref=e430]: Polity & Constitution              - generic [ref=e431]: \342\200\242 1 Statement (Factual Recall)            - generic [ref=e432]: \"Adaptive Level: Factual Recall (1 Stmt)\"          - paragraph [ref=e433]: Under Article 352 of the Constitution of India, within what period must a proclamation of National Emergency be approved by resolutions of both Houses of Parliament?          - generic [ref=e434]:            - generic [ref=e436] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e437]: A              - generic [ref=e438]: Within 1 month from the date of issue            - generic [ref=e440] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e441]: B              - generic [ref=e442]: Within 2 months from the date of issue            - generic [ref=e444] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e445]: C              - generic [ref=e446]: Within 6 months from the date of issue            - generic [ref=e448] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e449]: D              - generic [ref=e450]: Within 14 days from the date of issue          - button \"Check Answer\" [disabled] [ref=e452]        - generic [ref=e453]:          - generic [ref=e454]:            - generic [ref=e455]:              - generic [ref=e456]: Adaptive Q2              - generic [ref=e457]: Polity & Constitution              - generic [ref=e458]: \342\200\242 1 Statement (Factual Recall)            - generic [ref=e459]: \"Adaptive Level: Factual Recall (1 Stmt)\"          - paragraph [ref=e460]: Which Constitutional Amendment Act substituted the ground \'internal disturbance\' with \'armed rebellion\' for declaring National Emergency under Article 352?          - generic [ref=e461]:            - generic [ref=e463] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e464]: A              - generic [ref=e465]: 42nd Amendment Act, 1976            - generic [ref=e467] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e468]: B              - generic [ref=e469]: 44th Amendment Act, 1978            - generic [ref=e471] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e472]: C              - generic [ref=e473]: 52nd Amendment Act, 1985            - generic [ref=e475] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e476]: D              - generic [ref=e477]: 86th Amendment Act, 2002          - button \"