    combined_output {
      full: "<truncated 21 bytes>\n355]:            - generic [ref=e356]: \"UPSC CAPF Analytical Angle (Paper 1 & 2):\"            - paragraph [ref=e362]: Article 352 requires written recommendation of the Union Cabinet (ministers of cabinet rank), not merely the Prime Minister alone. Under Article 358, fundamental rights under Article 19 are automatically suspended only when emergency is declared on grounds of war/external aggression (not armed rebellion). Under Article 359, the President may suspend the right to enforce fundamental rights via court, BUT Articles 20 (protection against conviction) and 21 (right to life and personal liberty) can NEVER be suspended (44th Amendment Act 1978; Minerva Mills case 1980).          - generic [ref=e363]:            - generic [ref=e364]: \"SSC CPO Speed Formula / Mental Shortcut:\"            - paragraph [ref=e368]: \"30-Second CBT Rule: \\\"1-Month vs 2-Months\\\". Article 352 is the deadliest, so Parliament gets only 1 month to approve. Articles 356 and 360 are less urgent, so Parliament gets 2 months. Special majority is needed only for Art 352; simple majority suffices for Art 356 & 360.\"        - generic [ref=e369]:          - generic [ref=e370]:            - generic [ref=e371]: \"High-Yield Memory Hook / Mnemonic:\"            - paragraph [ref=e381]: \"Mnemonic: \\\"WAR-20-21-UNTOUCHABLE\\\" (Grounds: War, External Aggression, Armed Rebellion; Arts 20 & 21 can never be touched even during emergency).\"          - generic [ref=e382]:            - generic [ref=e383]: \"Classic Examiner Negative-Marking Trap:\"            - paragraph [ref=e387]: Examiners frequently swap \"written advice of Prime Minister\" for \"written advice of Cabinet\" (it MUST be Cabinet) and claim Art 19 is suspended during Armed Rebellion (it is NOT suspended during armed rebellion).        - generic [ref=e388]:          - generic [ref=e389]:            - generic [ref=e390]:              - generic [ref=e391]:                - heading \"Generate Practice Questions (Calibrated to Current Gap)\" [level=4] [ref=e392]                - generic [ref=e393]: 4 Statements              - paragraph [ref=e394]:                - text: \"Engine will generate questions specifically addressing:\"                - generic [ref=e395]: \"\\\"Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not correct\\\", \\\"only\\\")\\\"\"            - button \"Generate 4-Statement Drill\" [ref=e418]          - generic [ref=e400]:            - generic [ref=e401]:              - generic [ref=e402]: \"Select Statement Depth:\"              - generic [ref=e403]: 4-statement complex multi-layered constitutional analysis            - generic [ref=e404]:              - button \"1 Stmt (Factual Recall) Direct CBT Recall\" [ref=e405] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e406]: 1 Stmt (Factual Recall)                - generic [ref=e407]: Direct CBT Recall              - button \"2 Stmts (Foundational) Binary Contrast\" [ref=e408] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e409]: 2 Stmts (Foundational)                - generic [ref=e410]: Binary Contrast              - button \"3 Stmts (Standard UPSC) Standard Elimination\" [ref=e411] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e412]: 3 Stmts (Standard UPSC)                - generic [ref=e413]: Standard Elimination              - button \"4 Stmts (Complex Analysis) Multi-Combinatorial\" [ref=e414] [cursor=pointer]:                - generic [ref=e415]: 4 Stmts (Complex Analysis)                - generic [ref=e416]: Multi-Combinatorial      - generic [ref=e419]:        - generic [ref=e420]:          - \'heading \"Adaptively Calibrated Drill (4 Statements \342\200\242 Level: Advanced)\" [level=3] [ref=e424]\'          - generic [ref=e425]: \"Tuned to: Careless reading of negative qualifiers (\\\"not...\"        - generic [ref=e426]:          - generic [ref=e427]:            - generic [ref=e428]:              - generic [ref=e429]: Adaptive Q1              - generic [ref=e430]: Polity & Constitution              - generic [ref=e431]: \342\200\242 4 Statements            - generic [ref=e432]: \"Adaptive Level: Advanced (4 Stmts)\"          - paragraph [ref=e433]: \"With reference to the constitutional machinery during emergencies in India, consider the following statements:\"          - generic [ref=e434]:            - generic [ref=e435]:              - strong [ref=e436]: \"1.\"              - text: During a National Emergency, the Centre becomes entitled to give executive directions to a state on \"any\" matter, not merely limited to federal list subjects.            - generic [ref=e437]:              - strong [ref=e438]: \"2.\"              - text: The life of the Lok Sabha may be extended by Parliament by law for any period not exceeding one year at a time during a National Emergency.            - generic [ref=e439]:              - strong [ref=e440]: \"3.\"              - text: A resolution of disapproval of National Emergency can be passed by the Lok Sabha alone with a simple majority.            - generic [ref=e441]:              - strong [ref=e442]: \"4.\"              - text: During President Rule under Article 356, the State Legislative Assembly is automatically dissolved upon the proclamation.          - generic [ref=e443]:            - generic [ref=e445] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e446]: A              - generic [ref=e447]: 1, 2 and 3 only            - generic [ref=e449] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e450]: B              - generic [ref=e451]: 2, 3 and 4 only            - generic [ref=e453] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e454]: C              - generic [ref=e455]: 1 and 2 only            - generic [ref=e457] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e458]: D              - generic [ref=e459]: 1, 2, 3 and 4          - button \"Check Answer\" [disabled] [ref=e461]        - generic [ref=e462]:          - generic [ref=e463]:            - generic [ref=e464]:              - generic [ref=e465]: Adaptive Q2              - generic [ref=e466]: Polity & Constitution              - generic [ref=e467]: \342\200\242 4 Statements            - generic [ref=e468]: \"Adaptive Level: Advanced (4 Stmts)\"          - paragraph [ref=e469]: \"Consider the following statements regarding Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) and Article 33 of the Constitution:\"          - generic [ref=e470]:            - generic [ref=e471]:              - strong [ref=e472]: \"1.\"              - text: Article 33 confers power exclusively on Parliament to restrict the Fundamental Rights of members of armed and police forces.            - generic [ref=e473]:              - strong [ref=e474]: \"2.\"              - text: The expression \"members of the armed forces\" under Article 33 includes non-combatants such as cooks, carpenters, and tailors attached to the forces.            - generic [ref=e475]:              - strong [ref=e476]: \"3.\"              - text: A law enacted by Parliament under Article 33 excludes the writ jurisdiction of High Courts and the Supreme Court under Articles 226 and 32 respectively.            - generic [ref=e477]:              - strong [ref=e478]: \"4.\"              - text: Under Article 34, Parliament can indemnify any person in service of the Union or a State in respect of any act done in connection with the maintenance of order during martial law.          - generic [ref=e479]:            - generic [ref=e481] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e482]: A              - generic [ref=e483]: 1, 2 and 4 only            - generic [ref=e485] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e486]: B              - generic [ref=e487]: 1 and 3 only            - generic [ref=e489] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e490]: C              - generic [ref=e491]: 2, 3 and 4 only            - generic [ref=e493] [cursor=pointer]:              - generic [ref=e494]: D              - generic [ref=e495]: 1, 2, 3 and 4          - button \"Check Answer\" [disabled] [ref=e497]  - contentinfo [ref=e240]:    - generic [ref=e241]:      - generic [ref=e242]:        - generic [ref=e243]: DutyDeck        - generic [ref=e244]: \342\200\242 Dual-Target Preparation Engine for UPSC CAPF AC & SSC CPO      - generic [ref=e245]: Nordic Botanical Theme \342\200\242 15-Minute Section Gates \342\200\242 Elimination Scratchpad```Browser \'default\' closed"
