  planner_response {
    response: "### Statement Depth Configuration & Adaptive Engine Update\n\n1. **Statement Depth Configuration UI in AI Tutor**:\n   - Added a dedicated 4-way Statement Depth configuration bar directly inside `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`, allowing aspirants to manually choose their target question granularity across 4 distinct levels:\n     - **1 Stmt (Factual Recall)**: Single-statement direct CBT objective format (no statement list; direct options A\342\200\223D for rapid constitutional articles, amendments, and definitions).\n     - **2 Stmts (Foundational)**: High-contrast binary verification (Statements 1 & 2; \"1 only\", \"2 only\", \"Both 1 and 2\", \"Neither 1 nor 2\").\n     - **3 Stmts (Standard UPSC)**: Canonical 3-statement elimination format replicating standard UPSC CAPF AC Paper 1 questions.\n     - **4 Stmts (Complex Analysis)**: Multi-layered 4-statement constitutional and operational analysis with combinatorial elimination options.\n   - Wired live depth toggles in both the **Adaptive Learning Gap HUD** and the **Generate Practice Questions** trigger container with real-time status badges (`(Manual)` vs `(Auto)`).\n\n2. **AI Question Generation Logic & Fallback Engine**:\n   - Updated `/api/ai/generate-questions` in `server.ts` to respect `statementDepth: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4`.\n   - When `statementDepth === 1`, the prompt instructs the engine to output `type: \"SINGLE_CHOICE\"`, omit numbered statement arrays, and format direct question stems with 4 substantive choices.\n   - Implemented high-yield curated fallback questions for Statement Depth 1 covering high-frequency CAPF/CPO topics (e.g., Article 352 1-month approval window and the 44th Amendment Act).\n\n3. **Testing & Verification**:\n   - Added unit test cases in `src/utils/adaptiveEngine.test.ts` verifying prompt directive formation and single-statement rules. All 10 unit tests pass.\n   - Recompiled and linted with 0 errors (`compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passing).\n   - Executed headless browser automation verifying that selecting **1 Stmt** produces direct CBT factual questions with no statement bullets, while selecting **4 Stmts** produces 4-statement multi-layered UPSC elimination questions."
    modified_response: "### Statement Depth Configuration & Adaptive Engine Update\n\n1. **Statement Depth Configuration UI in AI Tutor**:\n   - Added a dedicated 4-way Statement Depth configuration bar directly inside `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`, allowing aspirants to manually choose their target question granularity across 4 distinct levels:\n     - **1 Stmt (Factual Recall)**: Single-statement direct CBT objective format (no statement list; direct options A\342\200\223D for rapid constitutional articles, amendments, and definitions).\n     - **2 Stmts (Foundational)**: High-contrast binary verification (Statements 1 & 2; \"1 only\", \"2 only\", \"Both 1 and 2\", \"Neither 1 nor 2\").\n     - **3 Stmts (Standard UPSC)**: Canonical 3-statement elimination format replicating standard UPSC CAPF AC Paper 1 questions.\n     - **4 Stmts (Complex Analysis)**: Multi-layered 4-statement constitutional and operational analysis with combinatorial elimination options.\n   - Wired live depth toggles in both the **Adaptive Learning Gap HUD** and the **Generate Practice Questions** trigger container with real-time status badges (`(Manual)` vs `(Auto)`).\n\n2. **AI Question Generation Logic & Fallback Engine**:\n   - Updated `/api/ai/generate-questions` in `server.ts` to respect `statementDepth: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4`.\n   - When `statementDepth === 1`, the prompt instructs the engine to output `type: \"SINGLE_CHOICE\"`, omit numbered statement arrays, and format direct question stems with 4 substantive choices.\n   - Implemented high-yield curated fallback questions for Statement Depth 1 covering high-frequency CAPF/CPO topics (e.g., Article 352 1-month approval window and the 44th Amendment Act).\n\n3. **Testing & Verification**:\n   - Added unit test cases in `src/utils/adaptiveEngine.test.ts` verifying prompt directive formation and single-statement rules. All 10 unit tests pass.\n   - Recompiled and linted with 0 errors (`compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passing).\n   - Executed headles