- **Paper 2 Subjective** (UPSC CAPF AC 200M)\n   - Displays Mastery Score %, Solved / Bank question ratio, Net Accuracy, and error taxonomy tags (Conceptual Gaps vs. Misread Questions vs. Calculation/Time Panic).\n   - Clicking any subject card instantly filters the granular topic matrix below.\n\n5. **Granular Syllabus Subtopic Matrix (17 High-Yield Topics)**:\n   - **Section Filter Tabs**: Quickly switch between `All Sections`, `Shared Core (CAPF & CPO)`, `UPSC CAPF Track`, and `SSC CPO Track`.\n   - **Live Search**: Instant keyword search across topics, standard books (*M. Laxmikanth*, *Spectrum*, *NCERT*), and constitutional concepts.\n   - **Direct Actions per Topic**:\n     - **\"Study with AI\"**: Launches the AI Syllabus Tutor with topic, subject, and chapter reference pre-loaded.\n     - **\"Elimination\"** or **\"Speed Drill\"**: Launches the appropriate test engine for that topic.\n\n6. **Aspirant Milestones & Service Badges**:\n   - Gamified badges that unlock as study milestones are conquered:\n     - \360\237\233\241\357\270\217 **Discipline Sentinel** (Unbroken daily streak)\n     - \360\237\216\257 **Elimination Maestro** (Multi-statement elimination mastery)\n     - \342\234\215\357\270\217 **Paper 2 Strategist** (Descriptive lab submissions scored by AI)\n     - \360\237\223\246 **Mistake Purifier** (SRS reviews cleared on schedule)\n     - \342\232\241 **Speed Sprinter** (Rapid-fire quantitative drills under 15m pressure)\n     - \360\237\216\226\357\270\217 **Centurion Aspirant** (50 dual-exam questions solved)\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Testing\n- **13 Unit Tests Passing**: Pure logic covered in `src/utils/analyticsEngine.test.ts`, `src/utils/rules.test.ts`, and `src/utils/adaptiveEngine.test.ts` via `node:test`.\n- **Browser Automation Verified**: Verified navigation via the top nav bar and the Overview dashboard, tested section filtering (`Shared Core` 6/17 topics), and confirmed that clicking **\"Study with AI\"** from the topic matrix auto-populates the AI Syllabus Tutor.\n- **Build & Lint**: Zero compilation and lint errors."
