  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Security Rules**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the `firestore.rules` file now, focusing on the eight pillars of hardened security rules. I\'ve started with `rules_version = \'2\';` and the basic `service cloud.firestore { match /databases/{database}/documents {` structure. My first step is implementing the global default-deny rule, as it\'s the fundamental pillar.\n\n\n**Implementing Helper Functions**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining helpful functions to make the rules more readable and maintainable. I\'ve got `isValidId`, `incoming`, `existing`, `isSignedIn`, and `isOwner` done, now. I\'m focusing on user profile validation, ensuring all the right keys exist, and that only allowed keys are present in the profile data. Now, I\'m working on the data type and size constraints for the properties.\n\n\n**Validating Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now deep in the validation logic, ensuring data conforms to strict rules before it\'s saved. I\'ve defined `isValidMistake` and `isValidSubmission` functions. The `isValidMistake` function checks required keys, data types, and allowed values for the \"mistake\" documents, paying close attention to data type and size constraints. The `isValidSubmission` function is similar, validating data within submitted documents, ensuring specific properties exist and that constraints are met.\n\n\n**Refining Rule Logic**\n\nI\'m now honing the access control for user-specific data. I\'ve defined rules for user documents, including the restrictions on listing users. I\'m focusing on the sub-collection `mistakes` as well, ensuring that the rules for access and validation are in place there, too. I\'ve updated the rules to validate that all the properties and sizes are what they should be.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_6396980026048500542"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"rules_version = \'2\';\\nservice cloud.firestore {\\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\\n    // 1. Global Catch-All Default Deny\\n    match /{document=**} {\\n      allow read, write: if false;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Global Validation Primitives\\n    function isValidId(id) {\\n      return id is string && id.size() > 0 && id.size() <= 128 && id.matches(\'^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\');\\n    }\\n\\n    function incoming() {\\n      return request.resource.data;\\n    }\\n\\n    function existing() {\\n      return resource.data;\\n    }\\n\\n    function isSignedIn() {\\n      return request.auth != null;\\n    }\\n\\n    function isOwner(userId) {\\n      return isSignedIn() && request.auth.uid == userId;\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidUserProfile(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'uid\', \'email\']) &&\\n             data.keys().hasOnly([\'uid\', \'email\', \'displayName\', \'photoURL\', \'streakDays\', \'solvedCount\', \'createdAt\', \'updatedAt\']) &&\\n             data.uid is string && data.uid == request.auth.uid &&\\n             data.email is string && data.email.size() <= 200 &&\\n             (!(\'displayName\' in data) || (data.displayName is string && data.displayName.size() <= 100)) &&\\n             (!(\'photoURL\' in data) || (data.photoURL is string && data.photoURL.size() <= 500)) &&\\n             (!(\'streakDays\' in data) || (data.streakDays is number)) &&\\n             (!(\'solvedCount\' in data) || (data.solvedCount is number));\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidMistake(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'id\', \'questionId\', \'selectedAnswer\', \'correctAnswer\', \'reason\', \'timestamp\', \'reviewCount\', \'nextReviewDate\']) &&\\n             data.id is string && data.id.size() <= 128 &&\\n             data.questionId is string && data.questionId.size() <= 128 &&\\n             data.selectedAnswer in [\'A\', \'B\', \'C\', \'D\'] &&\\n             data.correctAnswer in [\'A\', \'B\', \'C\', \'D\'] &&\\n             data.reason in [\'Conceptual Gap\', \'Misread Question\', \'Calculation/Time Panic\'] &&\\n             data.timestamp is number &&\\n             data.reviewCount is number &&\\n             data.nextReviewDate is number;\\n    }\\n\\n    function isValidSubmission(data) {\\n      return data.keys().hasAll([\'id\', \'userId\', \'topicType\', \'prompt\', \'content\', \'wordCount\', \'submittedAt\']) &&\\n             data.id is string && data.id.size() <= 128 &&\\n             data.userId == request.auth.uid &&\\n             data.topicType in [\'ESSAY\', \'ARGUMENT\', \'REPORT\', \'PRECIS\'] &&\\n             data.prompt is string && data.prompt.size() <= 500 &&\\n             data.content is string && data.content.size() <= 10000 &&\\n             data.wordCount is number &&\\n             data.submittedAt is number;\\n    }\\n\\n    // User Profile Document\\n    match /users/{userId} {\\n      allow get: if isOwner(userId);\\n      allow list: if false;\\n      allow create: if isOwner(userId) && isValidUserProfile(incoming());\\n      allow update: if isOwner(userId) && incoming().uid == existing().uid && isValidUserProfile(incoming());\\n      allow delete: if isOwner(userId);\\n\\n      // User Mistakes Subcollection\\n      match /mistakes/{mistakeId} {\\n        allow get, list: if isOwner(userId);\\n        allow create: if isOwner(userId) && isValidId(mistakeId) && isValidMistake(incoming());\\n        allow update: if isOwner(userId) && isValidId(mistakeId) && isValidMistake(incoming());\\n        allow delete: if isOwner(userId) && isValidId(mistakeId);\\n      }\\n\\n      // User Submissions Subcollection\\n      match /submissions/{submissionId} {\\n        allow get, list: if isOwner(userId);\\n        allow create: if isOwner(userId) && isValidId(submissionId) && isValidSubmission(incoming());\\n        allow update: if isOwner(userId) && isValidId(submissionId) && isValidSubmission(incoming());\\n        allow delete: if isOwner(userId) && isValidId(submissionId);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create secure firestore.rules for user profiles, mistake vault, and paper 2 submissions\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/firestore.rules\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating firestore.rules\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write hardened Firestore rules\"}"
