  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Positioning Authentication Element**\n\nOkay, I\'ve located the ideal spot for the Google Login button and user profile component: right next to the quick metrics bar in `Navbar.tsx`. The design will be consistent across both desktop and mobile views. When a user is not logged in, I envision a clear, distinct button for authentication. I will move on to exploring the styling of this button, to ensure that it aligns with the application\'s current design system.\n\n\n**Styling The Authentication Button**\n\nI\'ve crafted the Google Login button\'s styling. I\'ve used `className` and provided it with flexbox styling, along with padding, borders and rounded corners. I\'ve also incorporated hover effects and transitions. Furthermore, I\'ve used different colors for light and dark modes, consistent with the application\'s design system. I am satisfied with the current implementation.\n\n\n**Refining User Authentication Component**\n\nI\'ve finalized the component for user authentication. The logic now dynamically renders either the \"Sign in with Google\" button (when logged out) or the user profile and sign-out button (when logged in). The component neatly incorporates the user\'s photo or initials, name, and sign-out function, with styling that aligns with the application\'s overall design, with custom styling for authenticated and unauthenticated states.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_3887625425385946814"
      name: "view_file"
