    response: "### Google Login & Firebase Authentication Integration\n\nGoogle Authentication has been integrated into DutyDeck using Firebase Auth and Firestore.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n1. **Firebase Provisioning & Security Hardening**:\n   - Provisioned Firebase services via `fax.ProvisionFirebase` for Google Authentication and Firestore database (`gen-lang-client-0456258653`).\n   - Created `firebase-blueprint.json` specifying the data models for user profiles (`/users/{userId}`), Spaced Repetition mistake vault records (`/users/{userId}/mistakes/{mistakeId}`), and Paper 2 subjective submissions (`/users/{userId}/submissions/{submissionId}`).\n   - Authored and deployed strict `firestore.rules` enforcing the 8 pillars of hardened rules:\n     - Global default-deny catch-all rule.\n     - Document-level ownership checks (`request.auth.uid == userId`).\n     - Validation helper functions (`isValidUserProfile`, `isValidMistake`, `isValidSubmission`) with string size and regex constraints preventing update gaps and identity spoofing.\n     - Deployed security rules via `fax.DeployRules`.\n\n2. **Firebase SDK & Authentication Layer**:\n   - Initialized Firebase in `src/lib/firebase.ts` with runtime configuration loading from `firebase-applet-config.json`.\n   - Bound Firestore instance with the dedicated database ID `firestoreDatabaseId`.\n   - Implemented standard `handleFirestoreError` error-handling protocol.\n   - Initialized `GoogleAuthProvider` configured with `prompt: \'select_account\'` and `signInWithPopup`.\n\n3. **Authentication Context & UI Integration**:\n   - Created `src/context/AuthContext.tsx` providing `user`, `loading`, `signIn()`, and `signOutUser()` across the application tree.\n   - Added a **\"Sign in with Google\"** button in `Navbar.tsx` featuring the official Google G emblem.\n   - When signed in, the header displays the user\'s avatar image or initials, account name/email, and a single-click **Sign Out** button.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- **Unit Tests**: All 13 unit tests pass (`src/utils/rules.test.ts`, `src/utils/adaptiveEngine.test.ts`, and `src/utils/analyticsEngine.test.ts`).\n- **Compilation & Linting**: Built and linted with 0 errors via `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`.\n- **Browser Automation Verification**: Verified in headless Chromium that the Google login component renders cleanly in the navigation bar."
    thinking: "**Observing UI Details**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the \"Sign in with Google\" button. The clean design, the official Google logo, the border, and the hover state are all notable. It\'s built cleanly, and it really stands out to me. The details have been given careful attention.\n\n\n"
