  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Learning Implementation**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the practical implementation. I\'m thinking about a direct testing page, which raises questions about how users will actually learn and explore the material. I need to consider subject-wise organization, including all relevant NCERT chapters. My primary reliance is going to be on these chapters.\n\n\n**Defining Core Requirements**\n\nI\'ve been dissecting the user\'s needs, and the core requirement is clear: a comprehensive learning academy focused on NCERT materials. They want a study-first approach, not just drill and testing. I\'m focusing on the \"build, verify, critique, and fix\" loop, integrating a headless browser verification with Playwright for the Skill Check and frontend design, for comprehensive knowledge. I\'m also ensuring integration with Firebase, specifically their `ai-studio-dutydeckupsccapf-11de2bb8-3d03-41f4-b9b1-31ec81e6ffef` database.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Content Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed subject coverage, specifically Polity, Modern History, and Geography. For each, I\'m meticulously mapping NCERT chapters and standard books like M. Laxmikanth and Spectrum, aiming for a direct, comprehensive syllabus alignment. This ensures a study-first approach by the user, while minimizing unnecessary content repetition. The goal is a truly self-reliant learning hub for complete preparation.\n\n\n**Expanding Curriculum Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the curriculum scope, delving into specific subject areas. I\'m focusing on the intricacies of Geography, including drainage systems and monsoon mechanisms. Furthermore, I\'m integrating quantitative aptitude content for SSC CPO and CAPF P1 math, including comprehensive formula handbooks and mental shortcuts. In addition, Reasoning and General Intelligence will have conceptual blueprints and deduction trees for syllogisms and more. Finally, I\'m working on masterclasses for essay writing and report drafting in the subjective writing syllabus.\n\n\n**Refining Study Module Design**\n\nI\'m currently refining the study module. I\'m focusing on providing complete reading lessons that are comprehensive per chapter. These will include core text from both NCERT and standard books, with explanatory paragraphs. I am also developing specific notes like \"UPSC CAPF Analytical Note\" and \"SSC CPO Speed Note\". Interactive checklists, summaries, and mini-quizzes will also be integrated.\n\n\n"
