  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Library Types**\n\nI\'m working on defining the types for the Subjectwise Learning Library, focusing on `src/types/index.ts`. I\'ve started with a `LearningChapter` interface, including fields like `id`, `subject`, and `ncertBook`. I am aiming for type safety and clarity, so I have a foundation to build on.\n\n\n**Expanding Chapter Structures**\n\nI\'m now expanding the `LearningChapter` interface to include specific fields relevant to detailed textbook chapters. This involves incorporating properties for \"Spectrum Modern India,\" such as chapter number, title, read time, exam relevance, weightage, core concepts, and comprehensive sections. I\'m also adding fields like analytical angles, speed shortcuts, common examiner traps, high-yield mnemonics, and comprehension quizzes to make the chapters more useful.\n\n\n**Detailing Chapter Outlines**\n\nI\'m currently detailing the chapter outlines for the \"Indian Polity\" module, breaking each chapter down into its specific components and constitutional articles. I\'m focusing on \"The Constitution: Historical Background\" and \"Making of the Constitution, Salient Features, Preamble & Amendment\" from the \"Indian Polity\" module, and structuring them into sub-topics like the Historical Background (Regulating Act, Pitts India Act), and the constituent assembly (Committees, Objectives Resolution, Amendment, 44th Amendment, Basic Structure components). I want to ensure each chapter covers essential concepts.\n\n\n**Outlining Key Events**\n\nI\'m now outlining key events within each historical chapter, such as major leaders in the 1857 Revolt like Nana Sahib and Rani Lakshmibai. I\'m structuring chapter content for the Indian National Congress and Freedom Movement, covering phases from the Moderate phase to the Gandhian Era. I\'m including specific details on socio-religious reform movements and Government of India Acts. I\'m also focusing on key events during the Gandhian era.\n\n\n**Structuring Historical Outlines**\n\nI\'m structuring details for \"Subhas Chandra Bose, the INA & Military Mutinies,\" including the Azad Hind Fauj, Rani of Jhansi Regiment, 1945 Red Fort Trials, the 1946 Royal Indian Navy HMIS Talwar mutiny, and the Cabinet Mission Plan. I\'ve also outlined key events like the 1930 & Dandi Salt March, and the Quit India Movement in 1942. I am now working on geography and environment chapters.\n\n\n**Mapping Security Mandates**\n\nI\'m now mapping out strategic frontiers and operational mandates for CAPF units. I\'ve begun detailing India\'s international boundaries, like the Radcliffe Line, McMahon Line, and LAC, including their respective lengths and the CAPF units responsible for them. Key areas such as the Siliguri Corridor, Pangong Tso, and Doklam are also noted.\n\nI\'m also working on refining chapter outlines for compound interest versus simple interest, and have moved on to high-speed mental math, with formulas for 2 and 3 year deltas, as well as quarterly compounding adjustments. I am also working on topics such as effective annual rate. I have expanded into other quantitative aptitude chapters on speed, time, distance, and circular tracks with an eye to the relative velocity of vehicles in motion.\n\n\n**Structuring Aptitude Modules**\n\nI\'m now structuring chapters on quantitative aptitude and reasoning, like compound and simple interest, high-speed mental math, and time/work with pipes. I\'m focusing on syllogisms, Venn diagrams, and alphanumeric coding, along with direction sense and counter-argument writing for subjective exams.\n\n\n**Constructing Content Modules**\n\nI\'m now building modules for official report drafting and pr\303\251cis writing. I\'m focusing on headline creation, chronological event structuring with neutrality, and applying the one-third rule in pr\303\251cis writing to ensure concise summaries. I\'m also planning features like chapter completion tracking and reader mode controls for a better learning experience. I am updating `src/types/index.ts` with `LearningChapter` and `UserChapterProgress`.\n\n\n"
