  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: \"implement learning also its direct test page but how will user learn things explore all the topics subjects etc and build learning subjectwise all required ncert chpaters ad all i will only rely on this app so build it in that way\"\n   - **Core Objective**: DutyDeck was previously test/drill-heavy; the user wants to *completely rely* on this app for their preparation. Transform it into an all-in-one comprehensive study academy by adding a dedicated **Subject-wise Learning Hub / NCERT & Standard Textbook Academy** that lets aspirants explore and master all subjects and required NCERT/standard textbook chapters (NCERT Class 11 *Indian Constitution at Work*, M. Laxmikanth, NCERT *Themes in Indian History*, Spectrum, NCERT *Physical Environment*, Quantitative Aptitude, Reasoning, and Paper 2 Subjective Writing) before taking drills, with full text, diagrams, key takeaways, speed shortcuts, and mini-comprehension quizzes.\n   - **Target Exam Focus**: Dual-target UPSC CAPF AC and SSC CPO.\n   - **Dev URL**: `https://ais-dev-utbf4x2zob4afut6kbvudz-13080937602.asia-east1.run.app`\n   - **Firestore DB**: `ai-studio-dutydeckupsccapf-11de2bb8-3d03-41f4-b9b1-31ec81e6ffef`.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Previously Completed & Verified**:\n     - Google Login integrated via Firebase Authentication (`src/lib/firebase.ts`, `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`, `Navbar.tsx`). Rules deployed to Firestore via `fax.DeployRules`.\n     - Immersive Analytics & Study Matrix (`src/components/AnalyticsPanel.tsx`, `src/utils/analyticsEngine.ts`) with 13 passing unit tests and browser screenshots.\n     - Dual-mode CBT Speed sprint (15m sectional gate, >45s alert) and CAPF multi-statement elimination engine with scratchpad.\n     - Statement depth configuration (1, 2, 3, 4 statements) in AI Tutor and server question generator.\n   - **Completed in this turn**:\n     - `src/types/index.ts`: Added `LearningChapter`, `ChapterSection`, `ChapterQuizItem`, and `ChapterProgress` interfaces.\n     - `src/data/learningLibrary.ts`: Created comprehensive, rich chapter lessons with textbook content, tables, bullet points, UPSC CAPF analytical notes, SSC CPO speed shortcuts, examiner traps, mnemonics, and self-check quizzes covering Polity & Constitution, Modern History, Geography & Environment, Quantitative Aptitude, Reasoning & Intelligence, and Paper 2 Subjective Writing.\n   - **In Progress / Next to Build**:\n     - Create `src/components/LearningHub.tsx` (the comprehensive reading and study UI with subject filters, NCERT chapter list, interactive reader view, font-size/focus mode controls, key concept checkboxes, mini-quizzes, and \"Mark Chapter as Studied\" progress persistence).\n     - Update `src/components/Navbar.tsx` to add `LEARNING` (`\'NCERT Study Hub\'`) to `NavTab`.\n     - Update `src/App.tsx` to manage `chapterProgress` in local storage and render `activeTab === \'LEARNING\'`.\n     - Add learning navigation triggers in `OverviewDashboard.tsx` and `AnalyticsPanel.tsx` (\"Start Learning Chapter\", \"Read NCERT Theory\").\n     - Add unit tests for chapter progress and completion metrics in `src/utils/learningProgress.test.ts`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - Aspirants preparing for both UPSC CAPF AC and SSC CPO need deep textual explanations to learn from scratch, not just 2-sentence summaries.\n   - Each chapter needs:\n     1. NCERT / Standard Book citation (e.g. *NCERT Class 11: Indian Constitution at Work Ch. 1 & 8*, *M. Laxmikanth Ch. 7*, *Spectrum Ch. 15-23*).\n     2. Rich multi-section textbook explanation with structured tables (e.g. Constituent Assembly Committees, 1919 vs 1935 Acts comparison, Indian Border guarding forces table).\n     3. Dual exam callout boxes: \"UPSC CAPF Analytical Angle\" vs \"SSC CPO Speed Formula / Shortcut\".\n     4. Interactive self-check comprehension quiz (2\342\200\2233 questions per chapter).\n     5. \"Mark as Completed\" button so users see their % syllabus completion bar rise.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes (Exhaustive)**\n   - *Error 1 (earlier)*: `replace_file_content` target content not unique in `src/types/index.ts` due to duplicate blank lines at EOF.\n     - *Fix*: Viewed lines 130-142 with `view_file` to get exact unique context around `AdaptiveAssessment` and replaced cleanly.\n   - *Error 2 (earlier)*: Playwright strict mode multi-element match when clicking button text \"Analytics\".\n     - *Fix*: Targeted specific disambiguated button text `button:has-text(\"Full Analytics & Matrix\")`.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server runs on port 3000 via `server.ts` (`tsx server.ts`).\n   - `src/data/learningLibrary.ts` has full chapter objects ready for import.\n   - `src/types/index.ts` has `LearningChapter` and `ChapterProgress` exported.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Create `src/components/LearningHub.tsx`**:\n      - Sidebar / grid of subjects: Polity, Modern History, Geography & Border Security, Quant, Reasoning, Paper 2.\n      - Chapter explorer displaying NCERT book name, read time, weightage badge, and progress status (Completed / Unread).\n      - Interactive Reading Desk:\n        - Header with chapter title, NCERT book tag, and \"Mark as Mastered\" toggle.\n        - Reader controls: font size adjustments, reading progress bar, focus mode toggle.\n        - Rich sections with subheadings, styled callouts, and comparison tables.\n        - Dual Exam Strategic Notes (CAPF Analytical vs CPO Speed).\n        - High-Yield Examiner Traps & Mnemonics callouts.\n        - Interactive in-lesson Comprehension Quiz with immediate feedback.\n        - Action CTAs: \"Practice Elimination MCQs on this Chapter\", \"Deconstruct in AI Tutor\".\n   2. **Update `src/components/Navbar.tsx`**:\n      - Add `\'LEARNING\'` to `NavTab` with label `\'NCERT Study Hub\'`, icon `BookOpen`, and badge `\'Syllabus\'`.\n   3. **Update `src/App.tsx`**:\n      - Add `chapterProgress: Record<string, boolean>` state (with `localStorage` persistence).\n      - Wire `activeTab === \'LEARNING\'` to render `<LearningHub />`.\n      - Allow passing a selected chapter from other views (`onSelectChapter`).\n   4. **Update `OverviewDashboard.tsx` & `AnalyticsPanel.tsx`**:\n      - Add \"Start NCERT Chapter\" / \"Explore Study Hub\" buttons.\n   5. **Unit Tests**:\n      - Add tests in `src/utils/learningProgress.test.ts` verifying progress calculation and subject completion percentages.\n      - Run `npx --yes tsx --test`.\n   6. **Build & Lint Verification**:\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together.\n      - Run `restart_dev_server`.\n   7. **Browser Verification (`playwright-cli`)**:\n      - Open `http://localhost:3000`, click \"NCERT Study Hub\".\n      - Verify chapter browsing, reading lesson view, comprehension quiz interaction, and \"Mark as Mastered\" toggle.\n      - Capture screenshots into `.playwright-cli/r23-learning-hub.png`.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Maintain Nordic Botanical styling (`#36624B`, `#E3EFE8`, `#1E252B`, `#F7F8F5`, `#D97746`).\n   - Pure logic verified via `node:test`.\n   - Dev server must run on port 3000.\n   - Do not use alert/confirm dialogs in UI.\n</summary>"
