  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing the Learning Hub**\n\nI\'m now diving into the development of the Learning Hub ecosystem. Specifically, I\'m focusing on `src/utils/learningProgress.ts`. This will involve crafting pure functions. I\'m starting with calculating overall subject progress from chapter data and progress maps, including stats for total reading.\n\n\n**Refining Functionality Details**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the utility functions in `src/utils/learningProgress.ts`. I\'m focusing on `filterChapters`, ensuring it handles various filtering scenarios. I\'m also working on `getNextRecommendedChapter`, factoring in user mistake topics. The plan is to create thorough unit tests in `src/utils/learningProgress.test.ts`. After that, I will move on to the implementation in `src/components/LearningHub.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing the Presentation Layer**\n\nI\'m now detailing the visual elements for each chapter. I\'m focusing on the individual chapter components within the Learning Hub, planning out the display of book citations, reading times, and exam relevance indicators. Next, I\'ll be designing the main reading chamber\'s structure and controls, and I\'ll include chapter controls, such as font size and focus modes. Furthermore, I will create elements for quick progress updates, and a structured checklist of concepts. I will then structure the chapter\'s content with headings, explanations, and data tables.\n\n\n**Developing Strategic Insights**\n\nI\'m now focusing on strategic callout boxes. Specifically, I\'m designing dual-target exam callouts, including UPSC CAPF analytical angles and SSC CPO speed formula shortcuts. I will integrate high-yield examiner traps and mnemonics as well, like the *SOBS* for Preamble keywords. Finally, I\'m working on interactive quizzes for in-lesson comprehension.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4477574193910772113"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"ArtifactMetadata\":{\"RequestFeedback\":false, \"Summary\":\"Utility functions for calculating NCERT chapter progress, subject-wise completion rates, reading metrics, and AI recommendations based on user performance.\", \"UserFacing\":false}, \"CodeContent\":\"import { LearningChapter, ChapterProgress, Subject } from \'../types\';\\n\\nexport interface SubjectProgressStat {\\n  subject: Subject;\\n  totalChapters: number;\\n  completedChapters: number;\\n  completionPercentage: number;\\n  totalMinutes: number;\\n  completedMinutes: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LearningProgressSummary {\\n  totalChapters: number;\\n  completedChapters: number;\\n  overallPercentage: number;\\n  totalReadingMinutes: number;\\n  completedReadingMinutes: number;\\n  subjectStats: SubjectProgressStat[];\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Calculates comprehensive progress summary across all learning chapters\\n */\\nexport function calculateLearningProgress(\\n  chapters: LearningChapter[],\\n  progressMap: Record<string, ChapterProgress> = {}\\n): LearningProgressSummary {\\n  if (!chapters || chapters.length === 0) {\\n    return {\\n      totalChapters: 0,\\n      completedChapters: 0,\\n      overallPercentage: 0,\\n      totalReadingMinutes: 0,\\n      completedReadingMinutes: 0,\\n      subjectStats: [],\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  let totalMinutes = 0;\\n  let completedMinutes = 0;\\n  let completedCount = 0;\\n\\n  // Group by subject\\n  const subjectGroups = new Map<\\n    Subject,\\n    { total: number; completed: number; totalMins: number; completedMins: number }\\n  >();\\n\\n  for (const chapter of chapters) {\\n    totalMinutes += chapter.readTimeMinutes;\\n    const isDone = !!progressMap[chapter.id]?.isCompleted;\\n    if (isDone) {\\n      completedCount++;\\n      completedMinutes += chapter.readTimeMinutes;\\n    }\\n\\n    const current = subjectGroups.get(chapter.subject) || {\\n      total: 0,\\n      completed: 0,\\n      totalMins: 0,\\n      completedMins: 0,\\n    };\\n\\n    current.total += 1;\\n    current.totalMins += chapter.readTimeMinutes;\\n    if (isDone) {\\n      current.completed += 1;\\n      current.completedMins += chapter.readTimeMinutes;\\n    }\\n    subjectGroups.set(chapter.subject, current);\\n  }\\n\\n  const subjectStats: SubjectProgressStat[] = Array.from(subjectGroups.entries()).map(\\n    ([subject, data]) => ({\\n      subject,\\n      totalChapters: data.total,\\n      completedChapters: data.completed,\\n      completionPercentage: data.total > 0 ? Math.round((data.completed / data.total) * 100) : 0,\\n      totalMinutes: data.totalMins,\\n      completedMinutes: data.completedMins,\\n    })\\n  );\\n\\n  return {\\n    totalChapters: chapters.length,\\n    completedChapters: completedCount,\\n    overallPercentage: Math.round((completedCount / chapters.length) * 100),\\n    totalReadingMinutes: totalMinutes,\\n    completedReadingMinutes: completedMinutes,\\n    subjectStats,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Filter chapters by subject, search query, and exam track\\n */\\nexport function filterLearningChapters(\\n  chapters: LearningChapter[],\\n  filters: {\\n    subject?: string;\\n    searchQuery?: string;\\n    examTrack?: \'ALL\' | \'UPSC_CAPF\' | \'SSC_CPO\';\\n  }\\n): LearningChapter[] {\\n  const { subject, searchQuery, examTrack } = filters;\\n  const query = (searchQuery || \'\').toLowerCase().trim();\\n\\n  return chapters.filter((chapter) => {\\n    // Subject filter\\n    if (subject && subject !== \'ALL\' && chapter.subject !== subject) {\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Exam track filter\\n    if (examTrack && examTrack !== \'ALL\') {\\n      if (!chapter.examRelevance.includes(examTrack)) {\\n        return false;\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Search query matching\\n    if (query) {\\n      const matchTitle = chapter.chapterTitle.toLowerCase().includes(query);\\n      const matchBook = chapter.ncertBook.toLowerCase().includes(query);\\n      const matchConcepts = chapter.coreConcepts.some((c) => c.toLowerCase().includes(query));\\n      const matchTraps = chapter.examinerTraps.some((t) => t.toLowerCase().includes(query));\\n      const matchOverview = chapter.summaryOverview.toLowerCase().includes(query);\\n\\n      return matchTitle || matchBook || matchConcepts || matchTraps || matchOverview;\\n    }\\n\\n    return true;\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Suggests the next high-priority chapter to read\\n * Prioritizes:\\n * 1. Uncompleted chapters related to recent mistake subjects\\n * 2. Uncompleted \\\"Very High\\\" weightage chapters\\n * 3. First uncompleted chapter\\n */\\nexport function getRecommendedChapter(\\n  chapters: LearningChapter[],\\n  progressMap: Record<string, ChapterProgress> = {},\\n  weakSubjects: string[] = []\\n): LearningChapter | null {\\n  const uncompleted = chapters.filter((c) => !progressMap[c.id]?.isCompleted);\\n  if (uncompleted.length === 0) return chapters[0] || null;\\n\\n  // 1. Weak subjects matching\\n  if (weakSubjects.length > 0) {\\n    const weakMatch = uncompleted.find((c) => weakSubjects.includes(c.subject));\\n    if (weakMatch) return weakMatch;\\n  }\\n\\n  // 2. Very High weightage\\n  const veryHigh = uncompleted.find((c) => c.weightage === \'Very High\');\\n  if (veryHigh) return veryHigh;\\n\\n  // 3. First uncompleted\\n  return uncompleted[0];\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create learning progress and chapter filtering helper functions\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/learningProgress.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating learning helper\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write learningProgress.ts\"}"
