  planner_response {
    response: "### What was built & delivered\n\nThe requested **Subject-wise NCERT & Standard Textbook Academy (\"NCERT Study Hub\")** is now live, transforming **DutyDeck** from a drill-only app into a complete, self-reliant preparation platform for dual UPSC CAPF AC & SSC CPO aspirants.\n\n---\n\n### Core Architecture & Features Added\n\n1. **Dedicated NCERT & Standard Textbook Study Hub (`src/components/LearningHub.tsx`)**:\n   - **Curriculum Library**: Full textbook lessons bridging foundational NCERTs (Class 11 & 12) with standard reference texts (*M. Laxmikanth*, *Spectrum*, *D.D. Basu*).\n   - **Subject Coverage**:\n     - **Polity & Constitution**: *NCERT Class 11 Indian Constitution at Work (Ch. 1 & 8)*, *M. Laxmikanth* Fundamental Rights & Armed Forces exceptions (Articles 33\342\200\22335), Emergency Provisions (Articles 352, 356, 360).\n     - **Modern History**: *NCERT Class 12 Themes in Indian History*, Government of India Acts (1909, 1919 Dyarchy vs. 1935 Provincial Autonomy), Subhas Chandra Bose, INA & Military Mutinies (1942\342\200\2231946).\n     - **Geography & Border Security**: *NCERT Class 11 Physical Environment*, India\'s 15,106.7 km land frontiers, \"One Border, One Force\" doctrine (BSF, ITBP, SSB, Assam Rifles), Siliguri Corridor, Sir Creek, Doklam.\n     - **Quantitative Aptitude**: High-speed arithmetic, compound vs. simple interest derivations, 30-second delta shortcut ($D = P \\cdot (R/100)^2$).\n     - **Reasoning & Intelligence**: Syllogisms Venn diagrams, Either-Or conditions, and possibility rules.\n     - **Paper 2 Subjective Writing**: Official UPSC CAPF Paper 2 Counter-Argument architecture (40 Marks: Context $\\to$ For $\\to$ Against $\\to$ Way Forward).\n\n2. **Interactive Reading Desk & Study Controls**:\n   - **Font Size & Focus Controls**: Distraction-free reading toggle and adjustable typography sizing (`A-`, `A`, `A+`).\n   - **Interactive Benchmark Checklists**: Aspirants can tick off core syllabus concepts as they study them.\n   - **Comparison Tables & Bulleted Notes**: Formatted reference tables (e.g. Drafting Committees, 1919 vs. 1935 Act, Central Armed Police Forces border demarcations).\n   - **Dual-Exam Strategy Callouts**:\n     - \360\237\217\233\357\270\217 *UPSC CAPF Analytical Angle*: Elimination traps, multi-statement trickery, and Paper 2 essay application.\n     - \342\232\241 *SSC CPO Speed Shortcut*: 10-second mental math formulas and rapid grammar rules.\n   - **High-Yield Examiner Traps & Mnemonics**: Highlights common misconceptions and memory devices (e.g., *\"BA-CH-PA-N MEIN M-B-A\"* for border length rankings, *\"US-JUDGE-RIGHTS\"*).\n\n3. **In-Lesson Self-Check Comprehension Quizzes**:\n   - Every chapter includes instant interactive check questions with immediate answer feedback, explanatory breakdowns, and a \"Try Again\" retry feature.\n\n4. **Progress Persistence & Exam Synergy**:\n   - **\"Mark as Mastered\" Tracking**: Live calculation of syllabus completion percentage and reading hours logged in local storage.\n   - **Integrated Navigation**: Access chapters directly from the top navigation bar, the Dual Overview dashboard banner, or the Analytics Panel recommendation cards.\n   - **Direct Drill CTAs**: After reading any lesson, aspirants can launch directly into either the *CAPF Elimination Mode* or the *CPO Speed Mode*.\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Testing\n- **Unit Testing**: 17 unit tests passed cleanly via `node:test` (`src/utils/learningProgress.test.ts`, `analyticsEngine.test.ts`, `adaptiveEngine.test.ts`, `dutyDeckEngine.test.ts`).\n- **Build & TypeScript Check**: Both `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passed with zero errors.\n- **Browser Automation Verification**: Verified live in Playwright CLI with interaction through chapter navigation, reading desk controls, question selection, and progress toggling."
    modified_response: "### What was built & delivered\n\nThe requested **Subject-wise NCERT & Standard Textbook Academy (\"NCERT Study Hub\")** is now live, transforming **DutyDeck** from a drill-only app into a complete, self-reliant preparation platform for dual UPSC CAPF AC & SSC CPO aspirants.\n\n---\n\n### Core Architecture & Features Added\n\n1. **Dedicated NCERT & Standard Textbook Study Hub (`src/components/LearningHub.tsx`)**:\n   - **Curriculum Library**: Full textbook lessons bridging foundational NCERTs (Class 11 & 12) with standard reference texts (*M. Laxmikanth*, *Spectrum*, *D.D. Basu*).\n   - **Subject Coverage**:\n     - **Polity & Constitution**: *NCERT Class 11 Indian Constitution at Work (Ch. 1 & 8)*, *M. Laxmikanth* Fundamental Rights & Armed Forces exceptions (Articles 33\342\200\22335), Emergency Provisions (Articles 352, 356, 360).\n     - **Modern History**: *NCERT Class 12 Themes in Indian History*, Government of India Acts (1909, 1919 Dyarchy vs. 1935 Provincial Autonomy), Subhas Chandra Bose, INA & Military Mutinies (1942\342\200\2231946).\n     - **Geography & Border Security**: *NCERT Class 11 Physical Environment*, India\'s 15,106.7 km land frontiers, \"One Border, One Force\" doctrine (BSF, ITBP, SSB, Assam Rifles), Siliguri Corridor, Sir Creek, Doklam.\n     - **Quantitative Aptitude**: High-speed arithmetic, compound vs. simple interest derivations, 30-second delta shortcut ($D = P \\cdot (R/100)^2$).\n     - **Reasoning & Intelligence**: Syllogisms Venn diagrams, Either-Or conditions, and possibility rules.\n     - **Paper 2 Subjective Writing**: Official UPSC CAPF Paper 2 Counter-Argument architecture (40 Marks: Context $\\to$ For $\\to$ Against $\\to$ Way Forward).\n\n2. **Interactive Reading Desk & Study Controls**:\n   - **Font Size & Focus Controls**: Distraction-free reading toggle and adjustable typography sizing (`A-`, `A`, `A+`).\n   - **Interactive Benchmark Checklists**: Aspirants can tick off core syllabus concepts as they study them.\n   - **Comparison Tables & Bulleted Notes**: Formatted reference tables (e.g. Drafting Committees, 1919 vs. 1935 Act, Central Armed Police Forces border demarcations).\n   - **Dual-Exam Strategy Callouts**:\n     - \360\237\217\233\357\270\217 *UPSC CAPF Analytical Angle*: Elimination traps, multi-statement trickery, and Paper 2 essay application.\n     - \342\232\241 *SSC CPO Speed Shortcut*: 10-second mental math formulas and rapid grammar rules.\n   - **High-Yield Examiner Traps & Mnemonics**: Highlights common misconceptions and memory devices (e.g., *\"BA-CH-PA-N MEIN M-B-A\"* for border length rankings, *\"US-JUDGE-RIGHTS\"*).\n\n3. **In-Lesson Self-Check Comprehension Quizzes**:\n   - Every chapter includes instant interactive check questions with immediate answer feedback, explanatory breakdowns, and a \"Try Again\" retry feature.\n\n4. **Progress Persistence & Exam Synergy**:\n   - **\"Mark as Mastered\" Tracking**: Live calculation of syllabus completion percentage and reading hours logged in local storage.\n   - **Integrated Navigation**: Access chapters directly from the top navigation bar, the Dual Overview dashboard banner, or the Analytics Panel recommendation cards.\n   - **Direct Drill CTAs**: After reading any lesson, aspirants can launch directly into either the *CAPF Elimination Mode* or the *CPO Speed Mode*.\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Testing\n- **Unit Testing**: 17 unit tests passed cleanly via `node:test` (`src/utils/learningProgress.test.ts`, `analyticsEngine.test.ts`, `adaptiveEngine.test.ts`, `dutyDeckEngine.test.ts`).\n- **Build & TypeScript Check**: Both `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passed with zero errors.\n- **Browser Automation Verification**: Verified live in Playwright CLI with interaction through chapter navigation, reading desk controls, question selection, and progress toggling."
