  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing the user\'s requested settings panel within `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. The primary task involves adding a toggle for \"Question Statement Depth\", with options for \"Simple\" and \"Detailed\". I\'m structuring the implementation to keep it clean and focused.\n\n\n**Defining Complexity Tiers**\n\nI\'m now defining the `QuestionComplexityTier` type, encompassing \"Simple,\" \"Moderate,\" and \"Complex/UPSC.\" The plan is to build a toggleable settings panel, possibly titled \"\342\232\231\357\270\217 Question Generation Settings,\" within `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. Within this, I want to allow selection of question statement depth: simple (direct recall), moderate (binary contrast), and complex/UPSC (analytical, multi-layered). There will also be an option to choose 3 or 4 statements for Complex/UPSC.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration Options**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed settings for question generation. I\'m focusing on defining how \"Simple,\" \"Moderate,\" and \"Complex/UPSC\" tiers will influence the `statementDepth`, `complexityTier`, and `complexityLevel` parameters. I\'m adding toggles for \"Trap Injector Directive,\" \"Question Count,\" \"Target Exam Mode,\" and \"Auto-Sync with Adaptive Gap,\" all within the settings panel. These settings will feed into the API call with the topic, subject, and exam data.\n\n\n**Integrating Parameters**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how parameters like `complexityTier` and `statementDepth` integrate with the `/api/ai/generate-questions` endpoint in `server.ts`. I need to ensure the AI generation prompt and system instructions are updated appropriately. I\'m taking the `req.body` into account and verifying that the structure is in place, and that the settings are being passed correctly.\n\n\n**Deducing Complexity Parameters**\n\nI\'m now implementing the logic to deduce `effectiveComplexityTier` and `statementDepth` from the request parameters and adaptive assessment data. I\'ve built the conditional structure to prioritize explicit `complexityTier` values, and fall back to inferring them based on `statementDepth` or `adaptiveAssessment` values. Finally, I\'m updating the system instruction and prompt to reflect the chosen complexity tier and statement depth.\n\n\n**Analyzing Tier Specifications**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the question generation rules based on `effectiveComplexityTier` and `statementDepth`. I\'m handling Simple questions with a single-statement, direct recall format, ensuring they are single-choice with a target time of under 30 seconds. Moderate questions get two high-contrast statements. I\'m working on the conditional logic that determines the question structure based on these parameters and the `diagnosedGap` and `targetTrap` values, including appropriate formatting for each tier.\n\n\n**Implementing Elimination Formatting**\n\nI\'m now integrating the multi-statement question format, which includes standard analytical elimination options. For the Complex/UPSC tier, I\'m focusing on incorporating precise qualifiers, statutory exceptions, and judicial doctrines to align with UPSC CAPF Paper 1 standards. The implementation will include a function to update the user prompt with the correct statement depth and format, while adhering to the specified complexity tier, ensuring subtle qualifiers, statutory exceptions, and landmark judicial doctrines are accurately reflected.\n\n\n"
