  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining API Parameters**\n\nI\'m in the process of adjusting `server.ts` to accommodate the `complexityTier` and `statementDepth` parameters. I\'m also updating the AI prompt and system instructions and modifying fallback logic to reflect these new inputs, with the parameters being either \'Simple\' or \'Moderate\' and the latter as an integer, respectively.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_9615616870411718643"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Update /api/ai/generate-questions to accept Question Statement Depth complexity parameters (Simple, Moderate, Complex/UPSC)\", \"EndLine\":225, \"Instruction\":\"Accept complexityTier and statementDepth, update system instruction and prompt\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"// 2. AI Question Generator: Personalized practice questions for learning gaps\\napp.post(\'/api/ai/generate-questions\', async (req, res) => {\\n  const { \\n    topic, \\n    subject, \\n    examTrack, \\n    specificGap, \\n    count = 3, \\n    adaptiveAssessment,\\n    complexityTier: reqComplexityTier,\\n    statementDepth: reqStatementDepth\\n  } = req.body;\\n  const requestedCount = Math.min(Math.max(1, Number(count) || 3), 5);\\n  const track = examTrack || \'UPSC_CAPF\';\\n\\n  // Determine Question Statement Depth Complexity Tier: \'Simple\' | \'Moderate\' | \'Complex/UPSC\'\\n  let effectiveComplexityTier: \'Simple\' | \'Moderate\' | \'Complex/UPSC\' = \'Complex/UPSC\';\\n  if (reqComplexityTier === \'Simple\' || reqComplexityTier === \'Moderate\' || reqComplexityTier === \'Complex/UPSC\') {\\n    effectiveComplexityTier = reqComplexityTier;\\n  } else if (reqStatementDepth === 1 || adaptiveAssessment?.statementDepth === 1) {\\n    effectiveComplexityTier = \'Simple\';\\n  } else if (reqStatementDepth === 2 || adaptiveAssessment?.statementDepth === 2) {\\n    effectiveComplexityTier = \'Moderate\';\\n  } else {\\n    effectiveComplexityTier = \'Complex/UPSC\';\\n  }\\n\\n  // Derive exact Statement Depth (1, 2, 3, or 4)\\n  const statementDepth: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 = (\\n    reqStatementDepth === 1 || reqStatementDepth === 2 || reqStatementDepth === 3 || reqStatementDepth === 4\\n      ? reqStatementDepth\\n      : effectiveComplexityTier === \'Simple\'\\n      ? 1\\n      : effectiveComplexityTier === \'Moderate\'\\n      ? 2\\n      : (adaptiveAssessment?.statementDepth && adaptiveAssessment.statementDepth >= 3 ? adaptiveAssessment.statementDepth : 3)\\n  );\\n\\n  const complexityLevel = adaptiveAssessment?.level || (\\n    effectiveComplexityTier === \'Simple\' ? \'Factual Recall\' :\\n    effectiveComplexityTier === \'Moderate\' ? \'Foundational\' :\\n    statementDepth === 4 ? \'Advanced\' : \'Standard\'\\n  );\\n  const targetTrap = adaptiveAssessment?.trapTypeToInject || \'None\';\\n  const diagnosedGap = adaptiveAssessment?.identifiedGap || specificGap || \'Reinforce core principles\';\\n\\n  try {\\n    const systemInstruction = `You are a senior question setter for UPSC CAPF AC and SSC CPO.\\nCRITICAL QUESTION STATEMENT DEPTH & COMPLEXITY DIRECTIVE:\\n- Complexity Tier: ${effectiveComplexityTier.toUpperCase()} (Simple / Moderate / Complex/UPSC)\\n- Statement Depth: EXACTLY ${statementDepth} numbered statement${statementDepth === 1 ? \'\' : \'s\'} per question.\\n- Diagnosed Learning Gap to Target: \\\"${diagnosedGap}\\\"\\n- Trap Directive: Inject \\\"${targetTrap}\\\" traps to train aspirant\'s weaknesses.\\n\\nExact rules by Complexity Tier & Statement Depth:\\n${\\n  effectiveComplexityTier === \'Simple\' || statementDepth === 1\\n    ? `- SIMPLE (Direct Factual Recall / Speed CBT Mode):\\n  * Provide EXACTLY 1 direct single-statement objective question (Direct CBT format).\\n  * Do NOT provide numbered statements (1, 2, 3). Set \\\"statements\\\" to an empty array [].\\n  * \\\"type\\\" MUST be \\\"SINGLE_CHOICE\\\".\\n  * Options must be 4 direct alternatives (A, B, C, D) answering the question directly.\\n  * Focus on exact constitutional articles, amendment years, institutional headquarters, or statutory provisions.\\n  * Pacing: <30 seconds per question.`\\n    : effectiveComplexityTier === \'Moderate\' || statementDepth === 2\\n    ? `- MODERATE (Foundational Binary Contrast):\\n  * Provide EXACTLY 2 high-contrast numbered statements (Statement 1 and Statement 2).\\n  * Options MUST be the classic binary elimination format:\\n    \\\"A: 1 only\\\", \\\"B: 2 only\\\", \\\"C: Both 1 and 2\\\", \\\"D: Neither 1 nor 2\\\".\\n  * Focus on clear binary distinctions, essential constitutional articles, and textbook definitions to eliminate foundational confusion.`\\n    : `- COMPLEX/UPSC (Analytical Multi-Layered Elimination):\\n  * Provide EXACTLY ${statementDepth >= 4 ? 4 : 3} multi-layered numbered statements (${statementDepth >= 4 ? \'1, 2, 3, and 4\' : \'1, 2, and 3\'}).\\n  * Canonical UPSC CAPF AC multi-statement analytical elimination format.\\n  * Statements must contain subtle qualifiers (\\\"only\\\", \\\"exclusive\\\"), statutory exceptions (e.g. Art 33-35, Art 358 vs 359), and landmark judicial doctrines.\\n  * Options must test elimination heuristics (e.g. \\\"1 and 2 only\\\", \\\"2 and 3 only\\\", \\\"1, 2 and 3\\\", or \\\"1, 2, 3 and 4\\\").`\\n}`;\\n\\n    const prompt = `Generate ${requestedCount} practice questions strictly adhering to the candidate\'s complexity parameters:\\nTopic: \\\"${topic}\\\"\\nSubject: \\\"${subject || \'General Studies\'}\\\"\\nTarget Exam Track: \\\"${track}\\\"\\nQuestion Statement Depth: ${statementDepth} statements\\nComplexity Tier: \\\"${effectiveComplexityTier}\\\" (Parameters: Simple = 1 Stmt Direct, Moderate = 2 Stmts Binary, Complex/UPSC = 3-4 Stmts Analytical)\\nSpecific Learning Gap: \\\"${diagnosedGap}\\\"`;\\n\\n    const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-3.8-flash\',\\n      contents: prompt,\", \"StartLine\":175, \"TargetContent\":\"// 2. AI Question Generator: Personalized practice questions for learning gaps\\napp.post(\'/api/ai/generate-questions\', async (req, res) => {\\n  const { topic, subject, examTrack, specificGap, count = 3, adaptiveAssessment } = req.body;\\n  const requestedCount = Math.min(Math.max(1, Number(count) || 3), 5);\\n  const track = examTrack || \'UPSC_CAPF\';\\n\\n  const statementDepth = adaptiveAssessment?.statementDepth || 3;\\n  const complexityLevel = adaptiveAssessment?.level || \'Standard\';\\n  const targetTrap = adaptiveAssessment?.trapTypeToInject || \'None\';\\n  const diagnosedGap = adaptiveAssessment?.identifiedGap || specificGap || \'Reinforce core principles\';\\n\\n  try {\\n    const systemInstruction = `You are a senior question setter for UPSC CAPF AC and SSC CPO.\\nCRITICAL ADAPTIVE CALIBRATION DIRECTIVE:\\n- Complexity Level: ${complexityLevel.toUpperCase()}\\n- Statement Depth: EXACTLY ${statementDepth} numbered statements per UPSC multi-statement question.\\n- Diagnosed Learning Gap to Target: \\\"${diagnosedGap}\\\"\\n- Trap Directive: Inject \\\"${targetTrap}\\\" traps to train aspirant\'s weaknesses.\\n\\nRules per statement depth:\\n${\\n  statementDepth === 1\\n    ? `- FACTUAL RECALL LEVEL: Provide EXACTLY 1 direct single-statement objective question (Direct CBT format).\\n- Do NOT provide numbered statements (1, 2, 3). Set \\\"statements\\\" to an empty array [].\\n- \\\"type\\\" MUST be \\\"SINGLE_CHOICE\\\".\\n- Options must be 4 direct alternatives (A, B, C, D) answering the direct question.\\n- Focus on exact constitutional articles, amendment years, institutional headquarters, or statutory provisions.`\\n    : statementDepth === 2\\n    ? `- FOUNDATIONAL LEVEL: Provide EXACTLY 2 high-contrast numbered statements (1 and 2).\\n- Options must be: \\\"A: 1 only\\\", \\\"B: 2 only\\\", \\\"C: Both 1 and 2\\\", \\\"D: Neither 1 nor 2\\\".\\n- Focus on clear binary distinctions, essential constitutional articles, and textbook definitions to eliminate foundational confusion.`\\n    : statementDepth === 4\\n    ? `- ADVANCED LEVEL: Provide EXACTLY 4 multi-layered numbered statements (1, 2, 3, and 4).\\n- Cover subtle constitutional nuances, statutory exceptions (e.g. Art 358 vs 359, Art 33-35, Commission recommendations).\\n- Provide intricate elimination options (e.g. \\\"1 and 3 only\\\", \\\"1, 2 and 4 only\\\", \\\"2, 3 and 4 only\\\", \\\"1, 2, 3 and 4\\\").`\\n    : `- STANDARD LEVEL: Provide EXACTLY 3 numbered statements (1, 2, and 3).\\n- Canonical UPSC CAPF AC format with standard elimination patterns.`\\n}`;\\n\\n    const prompt = `Generate ${requestedCount} practice questions for:\\nTopic: \\\"${topic}\\\"\\nSubject: \\\"${subject || \'General Studies\'}\\\"\\nTarget Exam Track: \\\"${track}\\\"\\nAdaptive Depth: ${statementDepth} statements per question (Complexity: ${complexityLevel})\\nSpecific Learning Gap: \\\"${diagnosedGap}\\\"`;\\n\\n    const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-3.8-flash\',\\n      contents: prompt,\", \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating server prompt\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update /api/ai/generate-questions route in server.ts\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\373\a\n\370\a\001i\024}\023\247\301B\033\322%\306w\023;\325\375[\220R \t\033Cn\3711UG\233\226\234 A\316\n7jg\234\250\200s\360\362\017\257~\030\344d\320,\016\207\a\241\341\224*U\3459\370h`\005E\264>\225?\036\314o\n&\022\034\253W\221\327\036\337n\227\261\240\231\"\a\333=Sw\257U\367\302\262\312\242\363\375u8n\333\241\177\aB\356\342\034\036\024\304N\230-\365\022\037q\320\000/\251m\326\357\fmM\302w\267\305\272\357\263\021\022F\322\366g\337&\242\355s\2455\225u\357\371\360\017O\372c)\200i\240\253\217;\027\357\241\364w\367\302\232\303:\376b\261P|\\\n\364\030\247rx1\001\343\323#\214V\017\204\213\205\261Jfi\227\226\316\220\320\231Jdq\v}JN\214\vB\375\217\266\275\"\373\274;\352Lh\306J\006\303l\247WKT\316z\304\000\343\033\365xh<5U%a\324\037z\2453\n\303\n}v\332\354/b\246#\021\004CvNt)\000\030tC\256\220\300`\336~\214\272\"k2\024\v\237x\207\335W\366\303\327U\aq\005ji\333\363\302pG\362\220$\274\310;N\376gvf\212%#\005\035\305\340\345=@\370V\241V\027\b\2122\260\bR\376I\037\313n\330\t\000z\231\306\274V\327\t\213\243`7\377\026E\027\314\034\0313\022\354*.KH]\366h\362\367&M\257\"\005m\240\223\216=C\202|<H\326\006-\234\337\205\337\351I\377a]\321\3005P-\323\243\035&!\303j\354Q\277De\254P\030\3046\311\374\323\320p\304#\226N\022\372\311\374\213A\325\301\320R\202A\350s\376\311\377O\271Zl[\321\363O~\323N\025{\354~\351\373\026\340{]\241\352T\204l\335J\237\370#\216\347\030\031\315\221\207\270e7\316\224\026#\255*-\256]\235\035\210\025\343\265\373ls\006/U\022\256sZ\313h\026\3663\016aG\303\035#\316M\312AT\336o\377\017\321B\232\033\224\241\216\215\316\316l\277.d\225\216v\221\341\363l\264\246{1\206V10\250\317Q\334\027W\333`\261u\263(,;\303\320q+\230\25618\256h\321\226\3609tz\324k\211\303\267,\212}\324\002\177\313\211\345\224\\\203`\324\003\2079\213\261\202H\341\231I$\030@\335\'\225\033\257\2317\217\257\346\016\034\235\031\2136B{\231Gzs\346\353\031\305\350iv\307;\207x\004,\244\375\215\365)\"\360\'k\016a\206\027W\255[\213<\231<x\323c\r\2371\336\030\302\217p\332\363\bb[\34