  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Settings Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on integrating a settings panel within the AiTopicBreakdown component. The key feature is the \"Question Statement Depth\" toggle, allowing users to select Simple, Moderate, or Complex/UPSC levels. I\'m working to ensure the AI\'s behavior dynamically adjusts based on the selected depth setting, refining the AI.\n\n\n**Designing Settings Panel**\n\nI\'m now outlining the structure of the settings panel itself within `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. I\'m introducing state variables for toggling the panel\'s visibility, managing the complexity tier selection, and controlling statement depth, question count, and the inclusion of \"traps.\" I\'m also planning the logic to update these states based on user interaction with the complexity tier buttons, directly linking user selections to the complexity level.\n\n\n**Refining Complexity Tiers**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into refining the complexity tiers within the settings panel. I\'m focusing on clearly defining each level: Simple, Moderate, and Complex/UPSC. Each tier will have a label, a badge reflecting its core style, a tag summarizing its essence, and detailed descriptions that guide the user on its function within the AI\'s question generation. I am also working on naming the icon, expand/collapse toggle for clarity.\n\n\n**Implementing Advanced Options**\n\nI\'m now integrating advanced options within the settings panel for more precise control. For Complex/UPSC questions, I\'m adding a sub-selector for statement depth, differentiating between 3 and 4 statements. I\'m also including controls for practice question count and a toggle for \"Examiner Trap Injection,\" offering targeted traps like subtle qualifiers or factual distortions. Finally, a live prompt directive preview will display the exact prompts sent to Gemini, enhancing transparency. I\'m updating `handleGenerateQuestions` to accommodate these new parameters: `complexityTier`, `statementDepth`, `questionCount`, and `trapInjection`.\n\n\n"
