    thinking: "**Addressing the Alert**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx` file and flagged that pesky `alert(...)` on line 163. I\'m keen on replacing it, so I\'m thinking of setting an error state using `setGenerationError(err.message)` instead. This should keep things tidy and adhere to the server constraints.\n\n\n**Refining the Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the planned updates for `src/components/AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. My current focus is on structuring the imports and state management. I\'ve mapped out the necessary imports from `lucide-react` and decided on the state variables, including `complexityTier`, `manualDepth`, `showSettingsPanel`, `questionCount`, and `generationError`. I\'ve started the structure of the helper functions, specifically `handleToggleComplexityTier`, to manage the logic for complexity tier changes, and am almost done adding `isManualOverride`.\n\n\n**Structuring the Component**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the question generation settings panel within `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. The aim is to make it collapsible. I\'ve got the header bar and the basic structure of the card set up, including the `Settings` icon from `lucide-react`. I\'m using state to manage the visibility. I\'ve also implemented the logic to update `manualDepth` when `tier` changes to \'Complex/UPSC\'.\n\n\n**Implementing the UI**\n\nI\'ve been working on the UI of `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`, specifically on the display of the `complexityTier` and `manualDepth` information. I\'m focusing on making it user-friendly, including displaying the Active status, and providing the configuration parameters. I\'ve successfully added the configure/collapse functionality and incorporated the chevron icons to improve UX. I\'m making sure it\'s clear how to adjust the complexity level.\n\n\n**Refining the Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for the complexity tier selection within `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. I\'ve added labels and descriptions to improve clarity. I\'m focusing on making each tier distinct and visually appealing, using conditional styling to highlight the active tier, and I\'m ensuring smooth transitions to enhance the user experience. I\'ve also added inline descriptions to provide context.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Tier UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the UI for the \"Simple\" complexity tier within `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. I\'ve added a visual indicator to show which tier is active. The design includes a bold label, a small indicator dot, and a brief description for clarity. I\'ve also added inline descriptions to provide more context. The goal is to make it visually clear and intuitive for the user to understand the different complexity levels.\n\n\n**Evaluating Performance**\n\nI am now assessing the function\'s ability to extract specific details like constitutional articles, numbers, years, and speed formulas within a 30-second timeframe. I\'m focusing on the accuracy and efficiency of the response. The results are looking promising.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Component**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the complexity tier components in `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the visual representation of the \"Simple\" tier within the UI, using labels and descriptions to improve clarity. I\'ve been focusing on elements like the active indicator, the description, and making sure the information flow is clear.\n\n**Revising the Design**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual presentation of the \"Complex/UPSC\" tier in `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. I\'ve added a conditional style to highlight the active state and I\'m ensuring it is easily distinguishable within the UI. I\'ve focused on clarity, and the use of the indicator dot. I\'m also ensuring the contrast is optimal for both light and dark modes.\n\n\n\n**Refining the Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for the statement count selection within `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. I\'ve started on the sub-parameters section, focusing on how we present exact statement count options. I\'m adding a grid layout for the options and I\'m using state to manage the selected count to ensure a clear user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing the Grid**\n\nI\'ve got the statement count grid for `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx` almost finished. I\'m focusing on the visual feedback when options are selected, using a transition to show the active state. I\'ve also incorporated a conditional style for visual clarity.\n\n\n**Implementing the Options**\n\nI\'m now integrating the question count options directly into `AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. I\'ve added the buttons for selecting the number of questions to generate. I\'m focusing on the visual feedback and styling for the selected state. Currently working on the implementation of the `onClick` handler and the associated state updates.\n\n\n\n"
