  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Component Imports**\n\nI\'m currently updating `src/components/AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`. The first step involved refining the imports. I\'ve added `Settings`, `ChevronDown`, `ChevronUp`, and `SlidersHorizontal` from `lucide-react` to enhance the component\'s UI elements. I also imported `QuestionComplexityTier` from `../types` for improved type safety and data handling.\n\n\n**Implementing State Hooks**\n\nI\'ve just added several state hooks. Specifically, I\'m now managing `showSettingsPanel`, `complexityTier`, `manualDepth`, `questionCount`, and `generationError` using the `useState` hook. These hooks will drive the UI\'s dynamic behavior. I\'m storing `complexityTier` as a string type from `QuestionComplexityTier`. I\'ve also implemented the logic for `handleToggleComplexityTier`, which updates `complexityTier` and `manualDepth` based on the selected tier, and added `effectiveAssessment`, using `isManualOverride`, to adjust complexity accordingly.\n\n\n**Calculating Assessment Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on dynamically calculating the assessment, considering both manual overrides and auto-assessments. I\'m crafting conditional logic to determine the `effectiveAssessment` based on manual depth and complexity tier selections. If a manual depth is set, it overrides the auto assessment. I\'m mapping statements like \"Simple\" or \"Moderate\" to the `complexityTier` accordingly. The logic handles the display of a user-friendly rationale.\n\n\n**Finalizing API Interaction**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the API interaction logic within `generatePracticeQuestions`. I\'m now sending the refined data, including `examTrack`, `specificGap`, `count`, `complexityTier`, `statementDepth`, and `adaptiveAssessment`, in the request. Error handling is also implemented with `try...catch` blocks to manage potential network issues or API failures. Finally, I\'m updating the component\'s state to reflect the question generation status and results, including error messages if things go wrong.\n\n\n\n"
