  planner_response {
    response: "### Summary of Changes\n\nA dedicated **Question Generation Settings Panel** has been added to the `AiTopicBreakdown` component, allowing aspirants to toggle and calibrate **Question Statement Depth** across three distinct complexity tiers, and the server-side AI generation engine has been updated to accept and enforce these parameters in both Gemini prompts and curated fallbacks.\n\n---\n\n### Key Implementations\n\n1. **Question Generation Settings Panel (`AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`)**:\n   - **Collapsible Settings Panel**: An expandable configuration card featuring a quick toggle between **Hide Settings** and **Configure Settings**.\n   - **Statement Depth Tiers**:\n     - **Simple (1 Statement)**: Single-statement direct objective questions (direct CBT format for high-speed recall; exact constitutional articles, numbers, years, and speed arithmetic).\n     - **Moderate (2 Statements)**: Binary contrast questions testing two numbered statements (1 & 2) with classic binary elimination (\"1 only\", \"2 only\", \"Both 1 and 2\", \"Neither 1 nor 2\").\n     - **Complex/UPSC (3\342\200\2234 Statements)**: Canonical UPSC CAPF Paper 1 multi-statement analytical elimination questions with subtle qualifiers (\"only\", \"exclusive\"), statutory exceptions, and multi-layered elimination patterns.\n   - **Sub-Parameter Controls**:\n     - Exact statement depth selector (`1 Stmt`, `2 Stmts`, `3 Stmts`, `4 Stmts`).\n     - Generation question count selector (`3`, `4`, `5` questions).\n     - Live **Prompt Parameter Preview** box showing the exact directives dispatched to the AI model (`complexityTier`, `statementDepth`, `count`, and targeted learning gap).\n\n2. **Updated AI Generation API & Prompt (`server.ts`)**:\n   - `/api/ai/generate-questions` now accepts `complexityTier` (`\'Simple\' | \'Moderate\' | \'Complex/UPSC\'`) and `statementDepth`.\n   - **Gemini System Instruction**: Explicit directives matching each complexity tier:\n     - *Simple*: Strictly sets `statements: []` and `type: \"SINGLE_CHOICE\"`, testing direct factual alternatives.\n     - *Moderate*: Enforces 2 numbered statements with standard binary choices.\n     - *Complex/UPSC*: Enforces 3 to 4 analytical statements with subtle qualifier traps and elimination options.\n   - **Prompt**: Formats the prompt with `Question Statement Depth: ${statementDepth}` and `Complexity Tier: \"${effectiveComplexityTier}\"`.\n   - **Curated Fallback Engine**: Accurately maps the requested complexity tier and statement count if the live Gemini API key is unset.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- **Compilation & Linting**: `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passed with zero errors.\n- **Unit Tests**: All 17 unit tests in `src/utils/*.test.ts` passed cleanly.\n- **Browser Automation Verification**: Verified live in Playwright CLI: toggled through Simple (1 Stmt), Moderate (2 Stmts), and Complex/UPSC (3-4 Stmts), verified active badges and prompt directive updates, and confirmed visual layout."
    modified_response: "### Summary of Changes\n\nA dedicated **Question Generation Settings Panel** has been added to the `AiTopicBreakdown` component, allowing aspirants to toggle and calibrate **Question Statement Depth** across three distinct complexity tiers, and the server-side AI generation engine has been updated to accept and enforce these parameters in both Gemini prompts and curated fallbacks.\n\n---\n\n### Key Implementations\n\n1. **Question Generation Settings Panel (`AiTopicBreakdown.tsx`)**:\n   - **Collapsible Settings Panel**: An expandable configuration card featuring a quick toggle between **Hide Settings** and **Configure Settings**.\n   - **Statement Depth Tiers**:\n     - **Simple (1 Statement)**: Single-statement direct objective questions (direct CBT format for high-speed recall; exact constitutional articles, numbers, years, and speed arithmetic).\n     - **Moderate (2 Statements)**: Binary contrast questions testing two numbered statements (1 & 2) with classic binary elimination (\"1 only\", \"2 only\", \"Both 1 and 2\", \"Neither 1 nor 2\").\n     - **Complex/UPSC (3\342\200\2234 Statements)**: Canonical UPSC CAPF Paper 1 multi-statement analytical elimination questions with subtle qualifiers (\"only\", \"exclusive\"), statutory exceptions, and multi-layered elimination patterns.\n   - **Sub-Parameter Controls**:\n     - Exact statement depth selector (`1 Stmt`, `2 Stmts`, `3 Stmts`, `4 Stmts`).\n     - Generation question count selector (`3`, `4`, `5` questions).\n     - Live **Prompt Parameter Preview** box showing the exact directives dispatched to the AI model (`complexityTier`, `statementDepth`, `count`, and targeted learning gap).\n\n2. **Updated AI Generation API & Prompt (`server.ts`)**:\n   - `/api/ai/generate-questions` now accepts `complexityTier` (`\'Simple\' | \'Moderate\' | \'Complex/UPSC\'`) and `statementDepth`.\n   - **Gemini System Instruction**: Explicit directives matching each complexity tier:\n     - *Simple*: Strictly sets `statements: []` and `type: \"SINGLE_CHOICE\"`, testing direct factual alternatives.\n     - *Moderate*: Enforces 2 numbered statements with standard binary choices.\n     - *Complex/UPSC*: Enforces 3 to 4 analytical statements with subtle qualifier traps and elimination options.\n   - **Prompt**: Formats the prompt with `Question Statement Depth: ${statementDepth}` and `Complexity Tier: \"${effectiveComplexityTier}\"`.\n   - **Curated Fallback Engine**: Accurately maps the requested complexity tier and statement count if the live Gemini API key is unset.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- **Compilation & Linting**: `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passed with zero errors.\n- **Unit Tests**: All 17 unit tests in `src/utils/*.test.ts` passed cleanly.\n- **Browser Automation Verification**: Verified live in Playwright CLI: toggled through Simple (1 Stmt), Moderate (2 Stmts), and Complex/UPSC (3-4 Stmts), verified active badges and prompt directive updates, and confirmed visual layout."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\216\002\n\213\002\001i\024}\023\032Q\260\365\334\362R\2365r\242\321\261\267\337\v\027\263\317C\276\r]\030J\300\341J\336>\267&[\261-\332\361Y/+\\\362meR\032P\026^\251\317\365\330U\237\251yg|\242\303\360\311\a[1\246\332\330\254\030\203\337\264\205\231\256fnK\343\227e\301\'>\235\'Cnb\223\205\325B\255\316\330S\3232\246\274\3127ro\322S\375\006\331\240\321\372\354\270\200\276|Y\a\323Ehc\345\257\342^.\350\276;bE\370\305\246\t]\017\317\273\370}\253\226\274E\342\020w\250\303\3274\'^\247sY\"\317E\321\005I\324@Z\371\2218\353\214\311A.\345\252\267\026\345\'6\266a\277\377\r\273\n\374=^\376\222]\260\210\345\341\243\202\215\353\027]\251\205\246\\\241\337m\266%\365\027\375\004\033\235\353\320\256\274\250\255E\205\337U\213 L3sMZz\337\215mo\002f<\031\332\261\350\364\314\364}j\270\377!w"
